window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/b016-b1a1810c7d2ec804.json"]={sha256:"b1a1810c7d2ec804098c23ca19a5ffe8166f613d9b5adf10eae89e267a8e0dcf",value:{"id":"b016","title":"雪梨港灣大橋","titleEn":"Sydney Harbour Bridge","category":"structures","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"雪梨港灣大橋是跨度 503 公尺的雙鉸鋼拱橋，拱頂高出水面 134 公尺，橋面同時承載公路、鐵路、自行車道與人行道，1932 年通車。本課從雙鉸拱的推力與荷載路徑出發，分析桁架深度變化、鉚接與支承銷，再拆解兩岸以 128 條隧道錨碇鋼索支撐半拱懸臂架設、1930 年拱頂合龍與 1932 年 96 輛機車的載重試驗，最後談鉚接細節的疲勞評估、大面積塗裝維護，以及作為工程遺產的修繕與交接。","summaryEn":"Sydney Harbour Bridge is a two-hinged steel arch spanning 503 m, its crown 134 m above the water, carrying road, rail, cycleway and footway since 1932. Starting from the thrust and load path of a two-hinged arch, the course examines varying truss depth, riveting and bearing pins, then the cantilever erection of each half-arch held back by 128 cables anchored in rock tunnels, the 1930 crown closure and the 1932 load test with 96 locomotives, ending with fatigue assessment of riveted details, painting of a vast steel surface and repair and handover of an engineering heritage structure.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、吊裝或張拉作業許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, lifting or stressing permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"st-arch-viaduct-sea","subcategoryTitle":"拱橋、高架橋與跨海通道","subcategoryTitleEn":"Arch bridges, viaducts and sea crossings","learningTrack":"structures","learningSubdiscipline":"st-arch-viaduct-sea","learningTags":["structures","st-arch-viaduct-sea","arch"],"architectureFamily":"arch","architectureNodes":[["砂岩橋台與支承銷","Sandstone abutments and bearing pins"],["雙鉸拱桁架","Two-hinged arch trusses"],["吊桿與橫梁","Hangers and cross-girders"],["公路與鐵路橋面","Road and rail deck"],["架設錨索與隧道","Erection cables and tunnels"],["塗裝、檢查與遺產紀錄","Painting, inspection and heritage records"]],"architectureEdges":[[3,2],[2,1],[1,0],[4,1],[4,0],[5,1],[5,2]],"diagram":{"type":"arch","labels":["砂岩橋台與支承銷","雙鉸拱桁架","吊桿與橫梁","公路與鐵路橋面","架設錨索與隧道"],"labelsEn":["Sandstone abutments and bearing pins","Two-hinged arch trusses","Hangers and cross-girders","Road and rail deck","Erection cables and tunnels"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"拱橋推力與溫度練習：取跨度 L = 503 m、拱矢 f = 120 m、總荷載 w = 700 kN/m。拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f) = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN，每側垂直反力 V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN；每側兩片桁架分擔，單一支承合力 ≈ √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN。若拱矢減為 110 m，H 升到約 201,300 kN，增加約 9%，說明矢跨比對推力很敏感。溫度方面，拋物線拱弧長 s ≈ L + 8f²/(3L) = 503 + 8×120²/(3×503) ≈ 579.3 m；升溫 30 °C 時弧長增加 Δs = 1.2×10⁻⁵×579.3×30 ≈ 0.209 m，跨度固定時拱矢增加 Δf ≈ 3L·Δs/(16f) = 3×503×0.209/(16×120) ≈ 0.164 m，與公開資料所說熱天拱頂升高約 18 公分同量級。數值為教學假設，不代表雪梨港灣大橋的設計計算。","textEn":"Arch thrust and temperature exercise: take span L = 503 m, rise f = 120 m and total load w = 700 kN/m. A parabolic arch has thrust H = w·L²/(8f) = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN and vertical reaction per side V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN; with two trusses per side, one bearing's resultant is about √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN. Reducing the rise to 110 m raises H to about 201,300 kN, about 9% more, showing how sensitive thrust is to the rise-to-span ratio. For temperature, the parabolic arc length is s ≈ L + 8f²/(3L) = 503 + 8×120²/(3×503) ≈ 579.3 m; a 30 °C rise lengthens it by Δs = 1.2×10⁻⁵×579.3×30 ≈ 0.209 m, and with the span fixed the rise grows by Δf ≈ 3L·Δs/(16f) = 3×503×0.209/(16×120) ≈ 0.164 m, the same order as the roughly 18 cm crown rise on hot days cited publicly. Values are teaching assumptions, not the design calculations of the bridge.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":13,"enrichmentVersion":13,"stages":[{"id":"b016-v13-s1","title":"工程背景、荷載與結構系統","titleEn":"Context, loads and structural system","description":"本階段聚焦「503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑」與「桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch\" and \"Truss depth and unbalanced loading\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b016-v13-01","title":"503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「雙鉸拱支承」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Two-hinged arch bearings” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雪梨港灣大橋由兩片平行的拱桁架組成，每片桁架只在兩端以鉸接支承在橋台上，屬於雙鉸拱：支點可以轉動但不能水平移動，因此拱的重量與橋面荷載主要以軸壓沿拱肋傳到支點，並在支點產生很大的水平推力，由兩岸的砂岩與混凝土橋台承受。橋面以吊桿懸掛在拱下，同時承載公路、兩條鐵路、自行車道與人行道；四座以花崗岩飾面的橋塔位於拱端，主要是建築與視覺作用，並不承擔拱的推力。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「雙鉸拱支承」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The bridge consists of two parallel arch trusses, each supported only by hinges at its two ends on the abutments, making it a two-hinged arch: the supports can rotate but not move horizontally, so the weight of the arch and deck travels mainly as axial compression along the ribs to the supports, producing a large horizontal thrust resisted by sandstone and concrete abutments on each shore. The deck hangs from the arch on vertical hangers and carries road lanes, two railway tracks, a cycleway and a footway; the four granite-faced pylons at the arch ends are mainly architectural and visual and do not resist the arch thrust. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Two-hinged arch bearings” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: For a parabolic arch the thrust is H = w·L²/(8f).","failure":"常見誤解：「雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「雙鉸拱支承」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Two-hinged arch bearings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-01-k1","title":"503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑","titleEn":"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch","text":"雪梨港灣大橋由兩片平行的拱桁架組成，每片桁架只在兩端以鉸接支承在橋台上，屬於雙鉸拱：支點可以轉動但不能水平移動，因此拱的重量與橋面荷載主要以軸壓沿拱肋傳到支點，並在支點產生很大的水平推力，由兩岸的砂岩與混凝土橋台承受。橋面以吊桿懸掛在拱下，同時承載公路、兩條鐵路、自行車道與人行道；四座以花崗岩飾面的橋塔位於拱端，主要是建築與視覺作用，並不承擔拱的推力。","textEn":"The bridge consists of two parallel arch trusses, each supported only by hinges at its two ends on the abutments, making it a two-hinged arch: the supports can rotate but not move horizontally, so the weight of the arch and deck travels mainly as axial compression along the ribs to the supports, producing a large horizontal thrust resisted by sandstone and concrete abutments on each shore. The deck hangs from the arch on vertical hangers and carries road lanes, two railway tracks, a cycleway and a footway; the four granite-faced pylons at the arch ends are mainly architectural and visual and do not resist the arch thrust.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch\" is correct?","options":["雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。","雪梨港灣大橋由兩片平行的拱桁架組成，每片桁架只在兩端以鉸接支承在橋台上，屬於雙鉸拱：支點可以轉動但不能水平移動，因此拱的重量與橋面荷載主要以軸壓沿拱肋傳到支點，並在支點產生很大的水平推力，由兩岸的砂岩與混凝土橋台承受。","拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。"],"optionsEn":["The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust.","The bridge consists of two parallel arch trusses, each supported only by hinges at its two ends on the abutments, making it a two-hinged arch: the supports can rotate but not move horizontally, so the weight of the arch and deck travels mainly as axial compression along the ribs to the supports, producing a large horizontal thrust resisted by sandstone and concrete abutments on each shore.","An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雪梨港灣大橋由兩片平行的拱桁架組成，每片桁架只在兩端以鉸接支承在橋台上，屬於雙鉸拱：支點可以轉動但不能水平移動，因此拱的重量與橋面荷載主要以軸壓沿拱肋傳到支點，並在支點產生很大的水平推力，由兩岸的砂岩與混凝土橋台承受。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The bridge consists of two parallel arch trusses, each supported only by hinges at its two ends on the abutments, making it a two-hinged arch: the supports can rotate but not move horizontally, so the weight of the arch and deck travels mainly as axial compression along the ribs to the supports, producing a large horizontal thrust resisted by sandstone and concrete abutments on each shore. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b016-v13-02","title":"503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「雙鉸拱支承」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Two-hinged arch bearings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f)。取 w = 700 kN/m（恆載加活載）、L = 503 m、拱矢 f = 120 m：H = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN；每側垂直反力 V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN。每側兩個支承各分擔一半，單一支承合力 ≈ √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN。w 與 f 為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: For a parabolic arch the thrust is H = w·L²/(8f). With w = 700 kN/m (dead plus live), L = 503 m and rise f = 120 m, H = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN, and the vertical reaction per side is V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN. Each side has two bearings sharing half, so one bearing's resultant is about √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN. w and f are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以桁架模型分析各種荷載排列下的弦桿與腹桿力，比較雙鉸拱的推力與支承反力；橋台的抗推力以岩盤承載與滑動檢核驗證；營運期以測量監測橋台與支承的位移，任何水平位移都會改變拱的內力分布。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Analyse chord and web forces under all load arrangements with a truss model, comparing two-hinged thrust and bearing reactions; verify abutment thrust resistance by rock bearing and sliding checks; in service monitor abutment and bearing movements by survey, since any horizontal movement changes the arch's internal forces.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f)。取 w = 700 kN/m（恆載加活載）、L = 503 m、拱矢 f = 120 m：H = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN；每側垂直反力 V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN。每側兩個支承各分擔一半，單一支承合力 ≈ √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN。w 與 f 為教學假設。","textEn":"For a parabolic arch the thrust is H = w·L²/(8f). With w = 700 kN/m (dead plus live), L = 503 m and rise f = 120 m, H = 700×503²/(8×120) ≈ 184,500 kN, and the vertical reaction per side is V = w·L/2 ≈ 176,000 kN. Each side has two bearings sharing half, so one bearing's resultant is about √(88,000² + 92,200²) ≈ 127,500 kN. w and f are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch\", which statement holds?","options":["鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。","兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f)。"],"optionsEn":["Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance.","The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","For a parabolic arch the thrust is H = w·L²/(8f)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拋物線拱推力 H = w·L²/(8f)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"For a parabolic arch the thrust is H = w·L²/(8f). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b016-v13-03","title":"503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「雙鉸拱支承」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Two-hinged arch bearings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以桁架模型分析各種荷載排列下的弦桿與腹桿力，比較雙鉸拱的推力與支承反力；橋台的抗推力以岩盤承載與滑動檢核驗證；營運期以測量監測橋台與支承的位移，任何水平位移都會改變拱的內力分布。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Analyse chord and web forces under all load arrangements with a truss model, comparing two-hinged thrust and bearing reactions; verify abutment thrust resistance by rock bearing and sliding checks; in service monitor abutment and bearing movements by survey, since any horizontal movement changes the arch's internal forces. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：評估或改建前應先依原設計與竣工資料畫出明確的荷載路徑圖，標示受力構件與非結構構件；任何鄰近橋台的開挖或隧道工程都要先檢核對橋台水平位移的影響並設監測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Before assessment or alteration, draw an explicit load-path diagram from original design and as-built records that separates structural from non-structural elements; any excavation or tunnelling near the abutments must first be checked for its effect on horizontal movement and monitored.","failure":"注意干擾：若橋台在推力下發生水平位移，拱跨增加、拱頂下沉，拱肋彎矩大幅增加；把橋塔誤當成受力構件而在改建時移除或加載，會干擾原有的荷載路徑判斷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: If an abutment moves horizontally under thrust, the span lengthens, the crown drops and rib bending rises sharply; mistaking the pylons for load-bearing members during alterations can confuse the actual load path. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以桁架模型分析各種荷載排列下的弦桿與腹桿力，比較雙鉸拱的推力與支承反力；橋台的抗推力以岩盤承載與滑動檢核驗證；營運期以測量監測橋台與支承的位移，任何水平位移都會改變拱的內力分布。","textEn":"Analyse chord and web forces under all load arrangements with a truss model, comparing two-hinged thrust and bearing reactions; verify abutment thrust resistance by rock bearing and sliding checks; in service monitor abutment and bearing movements by survey, since any horizontal movement changes the arch's internal forces.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"評估或改建前應先依原設計與竣工資料畫出明確的荷載路徑圖，標示受力構件與非結構構件；任何鄰近橋台的開挖或隧道工程都要先檢核對橋台水平位移的影響並設監測。","textEn":"Before assessment or alteration, draw an explicit load-path diagram from original design and as-built records that separates structural from non-structural elements; any excavation or tunnelling near the abutments must first be checked for its effect on horizontal movement and monitored.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch\"?","options":["以桁架模型分析各種荷載排列下的弦桿與腹桿力，比較雙鉸拱的推力與支承反力。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。"],"optionsEn":["Analyse chord and web forces under all load arrangements with a truss model, comparing two-hinged thrust and bearing reactions.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以桁架模型分析各種荷載排列下的弦桿與腹桿力，比較雙鉸拱的推力與支承反力；橋台的抗推力以岩盤承載與滑動檢核驗證；營運期以測量監測橋台與支承的位移，任何水平位移都會改變拱的內力分布。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Analyse chord and web forces under all load arrangements with a truss model, comparing two-hinged thrust and bearing reactions; verify abutment thrust resistance by rock bearing and sliding checks; in service monitor abutment and bearing movements by survey, since any horizontal movement changes the arch's internal forces. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b016-v13-04","title":"503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「雙鉸拱支承」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Two-hinged arch bearings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若橋台在推力下發生水平位移，拱跨增加、拱頂下沉，拱肋彎矩大幅增加；把橋塔誤當成受力構件而在改建時移除或加載，會干擾原有的荷載路徑判斷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"If an abutment moves horizontally under thrust, the span lengthens, the crown drops and rib bending rises sharply; mistaking the pylons for load-bearing members during alterations can confuse the actual load path. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：橋面以吊桿懸掛在拱下，同時承載公路、兩條鐵路、自行車道與人行道；四座以花崗岩飾面的橋塔位於拱端，主要是建築與視覺作用，並不承擔拱的推力。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: The deck hangs from the arch on vertical hangers and carries road lanes, two railway tracks, a cycleway and a footway; the four granite-faced pylons at the arch ends are mainly architectural and visual and do not resist the arch thrust.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若橋台在推力下發生水平位移，拱跨增加、拱頂下沉，拱肋彎矩大幅增加；把橋塔誤當成受力構件而在改建時移除或加載，會干擾原有的荷載路徑判斷。","textEn":"If an abutment moves horizontally under thrust, the span lengthens, the crown drops and rib bending rises sharply; mistaking the pylons for load-bearing members during alterations can confuse the actual load path.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「503 公尺雙鉸拱的荷載路徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Load path of the 503 m two-hinged arch\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若橋台在推力下發生水平位移，拱跨增加、拱頂下沉，拱肋彎矩大幅增加；把橋塔誤當成受力構件而在改建時移除或加載，會干擾原有的荷載路徑判斷。","拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","If an abutment moves horizontally under thrust, the span lengthens, the crown drops and rib bending rises sharply.","An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若橋台在推力下發生水平位移，拱跨增加、拱頂下沉，拱肋彎矩大幅增加；把橋塔誤當成受力構件而在改建時移除或加載，會干擾原有的荷載路徑判斷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"If an abutment moves horizontally under thrust, the span lengthens, the crown drops and rib bending rises sharply; mistaking the pylons for load-bearing members during alterations can confuse the actual load path. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b016-v13-05","title":"桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Truss depth and unbalanced loading: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-04"],"objective":"說明「拱肋桁架深度」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Arch truss depth” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"拱桁架在拱頂深約 18 公尺、在兩端靠近橋塔處深約 57 公尺。如果荷載完全均勻並與拱軸吻合，拱只受軸壓；但列車、車流只佔半跨時，拱會產生彎矩，由上下弦桿的拉壓差承擔。桁架越深，同樣彎矩造成的弦桿力越小，所以在彎矩較大的區域加深桁架是有效率的做法。溫度變化也會讓雙鉸拱產生內力與變形：公開資料指出，炎熱天氣時拱頂可升高約 18 公分。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「拱肋桁架深度」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The arch trusses are about 18 m deep at the crown and about 57 m deep at the ends near the pylons. If loading were perfectly uniform and matched the arch axis, the arch would be in pure compression; but trains and traffic on half the span cause bending, carried as a push–pull difference between top and bottom chords. The deeper the truss, the smaller the chord forces for the same moment, so deepening the truss where moments are larger is efficient. Temperature also causes forces and movement in a two-hinged arch: public sources note that the crown can rise by about 18 cm on hot days. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Arch truss depth” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：弦桿附加力 ΔN ≈ M/h。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Additional chord force ΔN ≈ M/h.","failure":"常見誤解：「拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「拱肋桁架深度」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Arch truss depth”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-05-k1","title":"桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載","titleEn":"Truss depth and unbalanced loading","text":"拱桁架在拱頂深約 18 公尺、在兩端靠近橋塔處深約 57 公尺。如果荷載完全均勻並與拱軸吻合，拱只受軸壓；但列車、車流只佔半跨時，拱會產生彎矩，由上下弦桿的拉壓差承擔。","textEn":"The arch trusses are about 18 m deep at the crown and about 57 m deep at the ends near the pylons. If loading were perfectly uniform and matched the arch axis, the arch would be in pure compression; but trains and traffic on half the span cause bending, carried as a push–pull difference between top and bottom chords.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Truss depth and unbalanced loading\" is correct?","options":["拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。","鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。","拱桁架在拱頂深約 18 公尺、在兩端靠近橋塔處深約 57 公尺。"],"optionsEn":["An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered.","Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.","The arch trusses are about 18 m deep at the crown and about 57 m deep at the ends near the pylons."],"answer":2,"explanation":"拱桁架在拱頂深約 18 公尺、在兩端靠近橋塔處深約 57 公尺。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The arch trusses are about 18 m deep at the crown and about 57 m deep at the ends near the pylons. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b016-v13-06","title":"桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載：定量估算","titleEn":"Truss depth and unbalanced loading: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拱肋桁架深度」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Arch truss depth” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：弦桿附加力 ΔN ≈ M/h。若半跨活載在某斷面產生 M = 400,000 kN·m：在桁架深 h = 30 m 處 ΔN ≈ 400,000/30 ≈ 13,300 kN；若同樣彎矩出現在拱頂 h = 18 m 處，ΔN ≈ 22,200 kN，增加約 67%。彎矩值為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Additional chord force ΔN ≈ M/h. If half-span live load produces M = 400,000 kN·m at a section where h = 30 m, ΔN ≈ 400,000/30 ≈ 13,300 kN; the same moment at the crown with h = 18 m gives ΔN ≈ 22,200 kN, about 67% more. The moment is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以影響線求各桿件在鐵路與公路荷載不同排列下的最大拉、壓力，並把溫度作用納入組合；評估時在代表性弦桿與腹桿量測應變，比較實測與模型在列車通過時的反應比例。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Use influence lines to find maximum tension and compression in each member for rail and road load arrangements, including temperature in the combinations; in assessment strain-gauge representative chords and web members and compare measured and modelled response ratios under passing trains.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"弦桿附加力 ΔN ≈ M/h。若半跨活載在某斷面產生 M = 400,000 kN·m：在桁架深 h = 30 m 處 ΔN ≈ 400,000/30 ≈ 13,300 kN；若同樣彎矩出現在拱頂 h = 18 m 處，ΔN ≈ 22,200 kN，增加約 67%。彎矩值為教學假設。","textEn":"Additional chord force ΔN ≈ M/h. If half-span live load produces M = 400,000 kN·m at a section where h = 30 m, ΔN ≈ 400,000/30 ≈ 13,300 kN; the same moment at the crown with h = 18 m gives ΔN ≈ 22,200 kN, about 67% more. The moment is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Truss depth and unbalanced loading\", which statement holds?","options":["弦桿附加力 ΔN ≈ M/h。","鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。","載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。"],"optionsEn":["Additional chord force ΔN ≈ M/h.","A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support.","A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"弦桿附加力 ΔN ≈ M/h。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Additional chord force ΔN ≈ M/h. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b016-v13-07","title":"桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Truss depth and unbalanced loading: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拱肋桁架深度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Arch truss depth” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以影響線求各桿件在鐵路與公路荷載不同排列下的最大拉、壓力，並把溫度作用納入組合；評估時在代表性弦桿與腹桿量測應變，比較實測與模型在列車通過時的反應比例。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Use influence lines to find maximum tension and compression in each member for rail and road load arrangements, including temperature in the combinations; in assessment strain-gauge representative chords and web members and compare measured and modelled response ratios under passing trains. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：拱橋評估必須包含半跨與偏心荷載排列及溫度組合，並列出每類桿件的最不利工況；量測資料應附溫度紀錄，避免把溫度內力誤判為荷載效應。","observationEn":"Site practice: Arch assessment must include half-span and eccentric load patterns with temperature combinations and list the governing case for each member type; measurement data should carry temperature records so thermal forces are not mistaken for load effects.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以均布荷載檢核，半跨受載時的弦桿反向力或腹桿受力可能被低估；受壓腹桿在反覆受力下若接頭鬆動，有效長度增加，挫屈強度降低。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Checking only uniform load can underestimate chord force reversals and web forces under half-span loading; if joints of compression web members loosen under repeated loading, their effective length grows and buckling strength falls. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以影響線求各桿件在鐵路與公路荷載不同排列下的最大拉、壓力，並把溫度作用納入組合；評估時在代表性弦桿與腹桿量測應變，比較實測與模型在列車通過時的反應比例。","textEn":"Use influence lines to find maximum tension and compression in each member for rail and road load arrangements, including temperature in the combinations; in assessment strain-gauge representative chords and web members and compare measured and modelled response ratios under passing trains.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"拱橋評估必須包含半跨與偏心荷載排列及溫度組合，並列出每類桿件的最不利工況；量測資料應附溫度紀錄，避免把溫度內力誤判為荷載效應。","textEn":"Arch assessment must include half-span and eccentric load patterns with temperature combinations and list the governing case for each member type; measurement data should carry temperature records so thermal forces are not mistaken for load effects.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Truss depth and unbalanced loading\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以影響線求各桿件在鐵路與公路荷載不同排列下的最大拉、壓力，並把溫度作用納入組合；評估時在代表性弦桿與腹桿量測應變，比較實測與模型在列車通過時的反應比例。","鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Use influence lines to find maximum tension and compression in each member for rail and road load arrangements, including temperature in the combinations.","As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以影響線求各桿件在鐵路與公路荷載不同排列下的最大拉、壓力，並把溫度作用納入組合；評估時在代表性弦桿與腹桿量測應變，比較實測與模型在列車通過時的反應比例。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Use influence lines to find maximum tension and compression in each member for rail and road load arrangements, including temperature in the combinations; in assessment strain-gauge representative chords and web members and compare measured and modelled response ratios under passing trains. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b016-v13-08","title":"桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載：失效診斷","titleEn":"Truss depth and unbalanced loading: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拱肋桁架深度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Arch truss depth” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以均布荷載檢核，半跨受載時的弦桿反向力或腹桿受力可能被低估；受壓腹桿在反覆受力下若接頭鬆動，有效長度增加，挫屈強度降低。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Checking only uniform load can underestimate chord force reversals and web forces under half-span loading; if joints of compression web members loosen under repeated loading, their effective length grows and buckling strength falls. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：溫度變化也會讓雙鉸拱產生內力與變形：公開資料指出，炎熱天氣時拱頂可升高約 18 公分。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Temperature also causes forces and movement in a two-hinged arch: public sources note that the crown can rise by about 18 cm on hot days.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以均布荷載檢核，半跨受載時的弦桿反向力或腹桿受力可能被低估；受壓腹桿在反覆受力下若接頭鬆動，有效長度增加，挫屈強度降低。","textEn":"Checking only uniform load can underestimate chord force reversals and web forces under half-span loading; if joints of compression web members loosen under repeated loading, their effective length grows and buckling strength falls.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「桁架深度變化與非對稱荷載」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Truss depth and unbalanced loading\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。","若只以均布荷載檢核，半跨受載時的弦桿反向力或腹桿受力可能被低估；受壓腹桿在反覆受力下若接頭鬆動，有效長度增加，挫屈強度降低。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.","Checking only uniform load can underestimate chord force reversals and web forces under half-span loading."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只以均布荷載檢核，半跨受載時的弦桿反向力或腹桿受力可能被低估；受壓腹桿在反覆受力下若接頭鬆動，有效長度增加，挫屈強度降低。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Checking only uniform load can underestimate chord force reversals and web forces under half-span loading; if joints of compression web members loosen under repeated loading, their effective length grows and buckling strength falls. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b016-v13-s2","title":"材料、構件與接合細部","titleEn":"Materials, members and connection details","description":"本階段聚焦「鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘」與「支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Steel, workshops and six million rivets\" and \"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b016-v13-09","title":"鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Steel, workshops and six million rivets: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-08"],"objective":"說明「鉚接接頭」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Riveted joints” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大橋鋼構總重約 52,800 公噸，其中拱約 39,000 公噸。承包商 Dorman Long 在北岸米爾森斯角設置兩座加工廠，把鋼板與型鋼加工成桁架構件，公開資料指出約八成的拱段鋼材由英國預先成形後運來。構件之間以鉚接連接，全橋約有六百萬顆手工打製的鉚釘：鉚釘加熱到紅熱後插入孔中打成頭，冷卻收縮把板件夾緊，主要以釘身受剪與孔壁承壓傳力。鉚接沒有現代高強度螺栓那樣可靠的預拉力，因此接頭的行為更依賴孔的精度與鉚釘填孔程度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鉚接接頭」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The steelwork weighs about 52,800 t, about 39,000 t of it in the arch. The contractor Dorman Long set up two workshops at Milsons Point on the north shore to fabricate plates and sections into truss members, and public sources say about four-fifths of the arch steel arrived pre-formed from England. Members were joined by about six million hand-driven rivets: each was heated red-hot, inserted and headed, shrinking as it cooled to clamp the plies, transferring force mainly by shank shear and bearing on the hole walls. Riveting lacks the reliable preload of modern high-strength bolts, so joint behaviour depends more on hole accuracy and how well rivets fill their holes. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Riveted joints” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：鉚釘直徑 d = 25 mm，面積 A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²；容許剪應力取 100 MPa，單剪容量約 49.1 kN，雙剪約 98.2 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: A rivet of d = 25 mm has A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²; at an allowable shear stress of 100 MPa it carries about 49.1 kN in single shear and 98.2 kN in double shear.","failure":"常見誤解：「鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鉚接接頭」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Riveted joints”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-09-k1","title":"鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘","titleEn":"Steel, workshops and six million rivets","text":"大橋鋼構總重約 52,800 公噸，其中拱約 39,000 公噸。承包商 Dorman Long 在北岸米爾森斯角設置兩座加工廠，把鋼板與型鋼加工成桁架構件，公開資料指出約八成的拱段鋼材由英國預先成形後運來。","textEn":"The steelwork weighs about 52,800 t, about 39,000 t of it in the arch. The contractor Dorman Long set up two workshops at Milsons Point on the north shore to fabricate plates and sections into truss members, and public sources say about four-fifths of the arch steel arrived pre-formed from England.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Steel, workshops and six million rivets\" is correct?","options":["大橋鋼構總重約 52,800 公噸，其中拱約 39,000 公噸。","鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。","鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["The steelwork weighs about 52,800 t, about 39,000 t of it in the arch.","Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.","Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"大橋鋼構總重約 52,800 公噸，其中拱約 39,000 公噸。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The steelwork weighs about 52,800 t, about 39,000 t of it in the arch. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b016-v13-10","title":"鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘：定量估算","titleEn":"Steel, workshops and six million rivets: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鉚接接頭」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Riveted joints” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：鉚釘直徑 d = 25 mm，面積 A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²；容許剪應力取 100 MPa，單剪容量約 49.1 kN，雙剪約 98.2 kN。傳遞 10,000 kN 構件力需 10,000/98.2 ≈ 102 顆鉚釘。直徑與容許應力為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: A rivet of d = 25 mm has A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²; at an allowable shear stress of 100 MPa it carries about 49.1 kN in single shear and 98.2 kN in double shear. Transferring a 10,000 kN member force needs 10,000/98.2 ≈ 102 rivets. Diameter and allowable stress are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：評估時以原始圖說核對接頭鉚釘數量與排列，並以敲擊、目視或超音波檢查鬆動鉚釘與鉚釘頭腐蝕；鋼材取樣做拉伸與衝擊試驗，確認當年鋼材的強度與韌性，作為容量計算的依據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: In assessment, check rivet numbers and layouts against original drawings, look for loose rivets and corroded heads by tapping, visual or ultrasonic checks, and test steel samples in tension and impact to establish the strength and toughness of the original steel as the basis for capacity.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"鉚釘直徑 d = 25 mm，面積 A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²；容許剪應力取 100 MPa，單剪容量約 49.1 kN，雙剪約 98.2 kN。傳遞 10,000 kN 構件力需 10,000/98.2 ≈ 102 顆鉚釘。直徑與容許應力為教學假設。","textEn":"A rivet of d = 25 mm has A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²; at an allowable shear stress of 100 MPa it carries about 49.1 kN in single shear and 98.2 kN in double shear. Transferring a 10,000 kN member force needs 10,000/98.2 ≈ 102 rivets. Diameter and allowable stress are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Steel, workshops and six million rivets\", which statement holds?","options":["兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","鉚釘直徑 d = 25 mm，面積 A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²。","百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。"],"optionsEn":["The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","A rivet of d = 25 mm has A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²; at an allowable shear stress of 100 MPa it carries about 49.1 kN in single shear and 98.2 kN in double shear.","A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鉚釘直徑 d = 25 mm，面積 A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²；容許剪應力取 100 MPa，單剪容量約 49.1 kN，雙剪約 98.2 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"A rivet of d = 25 mm has A = π×25²/4 ≈ 491 mm²; at an allowable shear stress of 100 MPa it carries about 49.1 kN in single shear and 98.2 kN in double shear. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b016-v13-11","title":"鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Steel, workshops and six million rivets: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鉚接接頭」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Riveted joints” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"評估時以原始圖說核對接頭鉚釘數量與排列，並以敲擊、目視或超音波檢查鬆動鉚釘與鉚釘頭腐蝕；鋼材取樣做拉伸與衝擊試驗，確認當年鋼材的強度與韌性，作為容量計算的依據。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"In assessment, check rivet numbers and layouts against original drawings, look for loose rivets and corroded heads by tapping, visual or ultrasonic checks, and test steel samples in tension and impact to establish the strength and toughness of the original steel as the basis for capacity. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：歷史鋼橋評估應先做材料試驗與接頭盤點，再決定容量計算的假設；發現鬆動鉚釘時以一對一的方式記錄位置與處置，替換方式需依保存原則與結構需求由工程與遺產雙方共同核定。","observationEn":"Site practice: Assessment of historic steel bridges should start with material testing and a joint inventory before fixing capacity assumptions; loose rivets are logged one by one with location and action, and replacement methods agreed jointly by engineering and heritage authorities according to conservation principles and structural needs.","failure":"注意干擾：鉚釘頭腐蝕或鬆動後，接頭夾緊力喪失，板件之間產生相對滑動與磨損，孔壁承壓集中而出現裂紋；若以現代鋼材性質假設評估百年前的鋼材，可能高估韌性，低溫下的脆性破壞風險被忽略。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Corroded or loose rivet heads lose clamping, letting plies slip and wear and concentrating bearing at hole edges until cracks form; assessing century-old steel with modern material properties can overestimate toughness and overlook brittle-fracture risk. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"評估時以原始圖說核對接頭鉚釘數量與排列，並以敲擊、目視或超音波檢查鬆動鉚釘與鉚釘頭腐蝕；鋼材取樣做拉伸與衝擊試驗，確認當年鋼材的強度與韌性，作為容量計算的依據。","textEn":"In assessment, check rivet numbers and layouts against original drawings, look for loose rivets and corroded heads by tapping, visual or ultrasonic checks, and test steel samples in tension and impact to establish the strength and toughness of the original steel as the basis for capacity.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"歷史鋼橋評估應先做材料試驗與接頭盤點，再決定容量計算的假設；發現鬆動鉚釘時以一對一的方式記錄位置與處置，替換方式需依保存原則與結構需求由工程與遺產雙方共同核定。","textEn":"Assessment of historic steel bridges should start with material testing and a joint inventory before fixing capacity assumptions; loose rivets are logged one by one with location and action, and replacement methods agreed jointly by engineering and heritage authorities according to conservation principles and structural needs.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Steel, workshops and six million rivets\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。","評估時以原始圖說核對接頭鉚釘數量與排列，並以敲擊、目視或超音波檢查鬆動鉚釘與鉚釘頭腐蝕；鋼材取樣做拉伸與衝擊試驗，確認當年鋼材的強度與韌性，作為容量計算的依據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value.","In assessment, check rivet numbers and layouts against original drawings, look for loose rivets and corroded heads by tapping, visual or ultrasonic checks, and test steel samples in tension and impact to establish the strength and toughness of the original steel as the basis for capacity."],"answer":2,"explanation":"評估時以原始圖說核對接頭鉚釘數量與排列，並以敲擊、目視或超音波檢查鬆動鉚釘與鉚釘頭腐蝕；鋼材取樣做拉伸與衝擊試驗，確認當年鋼材的強度與韌性，作為容量計算的依據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"In assessment, check rivet numbers and layouts against original drawings, look for loose rivets and corroded heads by tapping, visual or ultrasonic checks, and test steel samples in tension and impact to establish the strength and toughness of the original steel as the basis for capacity. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b016-v13-12","title":"鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘：失效診斷","titleEn":"Steel, workshops and six million rivets: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鉚接接頭」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Riveted joints” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"鉚釘頭腐蝕或鬆動後，接頭夾緊力喪失，板件之間產生相對滑動與磨損，孔壁承壓集中而出現裂紋；若以現代鋼材性質假設評估百年前的鋼材，可能高估韌性，低溫下的脆性破壞風險被忽略。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Corroded or loose rivet heads lose clamping, letting plies slip and wear and concentrating bearing at hole edges until cracks form; assessing century-old steel with modern material properties can overestimate toughness and overlook brittle-fracture risk. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鉚接沒有現代高強度螺栓那樣可靠的預拉力，因此接頭的行為更依賴孔的精度與鉚釘填孔程度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Riveting lacks the reliable preload of modern high-strength bolts, so joint behaviour depends more on hole accuracy and how well rivets fill their holes.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"鉚釘頭腐蝕或鬆動後，接頭夾緊力喪失，板件之間產生相對滑動與磨損，孔壁承壓集中而出現裂紋；若以現代鋼材性質假設評估百年前的鋼材，可能高估韌性，低溫下的脆性破壞風險被忽略。","textEn":"Corroded or loose rivet heads lose clamping, letting plies slip and wear and concentrating bearing at hole edges until cracks form; assessing century-old steel with modern material properties can overestimate toughness and overlook brittle-fracture risk.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「鋼材、工廠與六百萬顆鉚釘」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Steel, workshops and six million rivets\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["鉚釘頭腐蝕或鬆動後，接頭夾緊力喪失，板件之間產生相對滑動與磨損，孔壁承壓集中而出現裂紋。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["Corroded or loose rivet heads lose clamping, letting plies slip and wear and concentrating bearing at hole edges until cracks form.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鉚釘頭腐蝕或鬆動後，接頭夾緊力喪失，板件之間產生相對滑動與磨損，孔壁承壓集中而出現裂紋；若以現代鋼材性質假設評估百年前的鋼材，可能高估韌性，低溫下的脆性破壞風險被忽略。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Corroded or loose rivet heads lose clamping, letting plies slip and wear and concentrating bearing at hole edges until cracks form; assessing century-old steel with modern material properties can overestimate toughness and overlook brittle-fracture risk. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b016-v13-13","title":"支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-12"],"objective":"說明「支承銷與橋台」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Bearing pins and abutments” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雙鉸拱的鉸接點必須讓拱端自由轉動、同時傳遞巨大的推力與垂直力。雪梨港灣大橋每片桁架在每端以大型支承銷座在橋台的支承上，銷與銷座之間的接觸應力、轉動摩擦與潤滑決定鉸接是否真的像鉸。橋台把推力傳到砂岩岩盤，花崗岩飾面的橋塔則矗立在橋台上方，公開資料明確指出它們是建築性的、不承擔主結構荷載。鉸接若因腐蝕或磨耗而卡住，拱的實際行為會偏離雙鉸假設，溫度變化在支點處產生額外彎矩。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「支承銷與橋台」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The hinges of a two-hinged arch must let the arch ends rotate freely while transmitting huge thrust and vertical forces. Each truss end sits on a large bearing pin seated in abutment bearings, and contact stress, rotational friction and lubrication between pin and seat decide whether the hinge truly acts as a hinge. Abutments pass the thrust into sandstone rock, and the granite-faced pylons stand above them; public sources state clearly that they are architectural rather than structural. If corrosion or wear seizes a hinge, the arch departs from two-hinged behaviour and temperature changes induce extra moments at the supports. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Bearing pins and abutments” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：單一支承合力 R ≈ 127,500 kN（承前單元假設），若支承銷直徑 d = 0.37 m、承壓長度 l = 4.2 m，平均投影承壓應力 σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Taking a bearing resultant R ≈ 127,500 kN from the previous unit's assumptions, a pin of diameter d = 0.37 m and bearing length l = 4.2 m has an average projected bearing stress σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa.","failure":"常見誤解：「鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「支承銷與橋台」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Bearing pins and abutments”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-13-k1","title":"支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔","titleEn":"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons","text":"雙鉸拱的鉸接點必須讓拱端自由轉動、同時傳遞巨大的推力與垂直力。雪梨港灣大橋每片桁架在每端以大型支承銷座在橋台的支承上，銷與銷座之間的接觸應力、轉動摩擦與潤滑決定鉸接是否真的像鉸。","textEn":"The hinges of a two-hinged arch must let the arch ends rotate freely while transmitting huge thrust and vertical forces. Each truss end sits on a large bearing pin seated in abutment bearings, and contact stress, rotational friction and lubrication between pin and seat decide whether the hinge truly acts as a hinge.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons\" is correct?","options":["鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。","雙鉸拱的鉸接點必須讓拱端自由轉動、同時傳遞巨大的推力與垂直力。","鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。"],"optionsEn":["Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance.","The hinges of a two-hinged arch must let the arch ends rotate freely while transmitting huge thrust and vertical forces.","A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"雙鉸拱的鉸接點必須讓拱端自由轉動、同時傳遞巨大的推力與垂直力。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The hinges of a two-hinged arch must let the arch ends rotate freely while transmitting huge thrust and vertical forces. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b016-v13-14","title":"支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔：定量估算","titleEn":"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「支承銷與橋台」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Bearing pins and abutments” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：單一支承合力 R ≈ 127,500 kN（承前單元假設），若支承銷直徑 d = 0.37 m、承壓長度 l = 4.2 m，平均投影承壓應力 σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa。銷徑與長度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Taking a bearing resultant R ≈ 127,500 kN from the previous unit's assumptions, a pin of diameter d = 0.37 m and bearing length l = 4.2 m has an average projected bearing stress σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa. Pin diameter and length are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：定期檢查支承銷周圍有無腐蝕產物、磨耗痕跡與潤滑狀況，並量測拱端在不同溫度下的轉角，確認鉸接仍能轉動；橋台以精密測量監測水平與垂直位移，與歷史紀錄比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Inspect around the bearing pins for corrosion products, wear marks and lubrication, and measure arch-end rotation at different temperatures to confirm the hinges still turn; monitor abutment horizontal and vertical movement by precise survey against historical records.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"單一支承合力 R ≈ 127,500 kN（承前單元假設），若支承銷直徑 d = 0.37 m、承壓長度 l = 4.2 m，平均投影承壓應力 σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa。銷徑與長度為教學假設。","textEn":"Taking a bearing resultant R ≈ 127,500 kN from the previous unit's assumptions, a pin of diameter d = 0.37 m and bearing length l = 4.2 m has an average projected bearing stress σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa. Pin diameter and length are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons\", which statement holds?","options":["載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。","鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。","單一支承合力 R ≈ 127,500 kN（承前單元假設），若支承銷直徑 d = 0.37 m、承壓長度 l = 4.2 m，平均投影承壓應力 σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa。"],"optionsEn":["A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough.","As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.","Taking a bearing resultant R ≈ 127,500 kN from the previous unit's assumptions, a pin of diameter d = 0.37 m and bearing length l = 4.2 m has an average projected bearing stress σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa."],"answer":2,"explanation":"單一支承合力 R ≈ 127,500 kN（承前單元假設），若支承銷直徑 d = 0.37 m、承壓長度 l = 4.2 m，平均投影承壓應力 σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Taking a bearing resultant R ≈ 127,500 kN from the previous unit's assumptions, a pin of diameter d = 0.37 m and bearing length l = 4.2 m has an average projected bearing stress σ = R/(d·l) = 127.5/(0.37×4.2) ≈ 82 MPa. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b016-v13-15","title":"支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「支承銷與橋台」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Bearing pins and abutments” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"定期檢查支承銷周圍有無腐蝕產物、磨耗痕跡與潤滑狀況，並量測拱端在不同溫度下的轉角，確認鉸接仍能轉動；橋台以精密測量監測水平與垂直位移，與歷史紀錄比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Inspect around the bearing pins for corrosion products, wear marks and lubrication, and measure arch-end rotation at different temperatures to confirm the hinges still turn; monitor abutment horizontal and vertical movement by precise survey against historical records. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：支承鉸接應列為關鍵構件，訂定檢查週期、潤滑與防蝕程序，並以轉角與溫度的量測紀錄判斷是否仍有效；任何支承維修都要先評估施工期間的臨時荷載路徑並設停留點。","observationEn":"Site practice: Hinged bearings should be classed as critical components with set inspection intervals and lubrication and corrosion-protection procedures, judged effective by rotation-versus-temperature records; any bearing repair needs a prior assessment of the temporary load path and hold points.","failure":"注意干擾：支承銷卡滯時，雙鉸拱局部變成固定拱，溫度與活載在拱端產生原設計沒有考慮的彎矩，可能使端部桿件或接頭過應力；銷座腐蝕產生的膨脹也會改變接觸條件，造成應力集中。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: A seized pin turns the two-hinged arch locally into a fixed arch, so temperature and live load create end moments the original design never considered, possibly overstressing end members or joints; expanding corrosion in the seat alters contact and concentrates stress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"定期檢查支承銷周圍有無腐蝕產物、磨耗痕跡與潤滑狀況，並量測拱端在不同溫度下的轉角，確認鉸接仍能轉動；橋台以精密測量監測水平與垂直位移，與歷史紀錄比較。","textEn":"Inspect around the bearing pins for corrosion products, wear marks and lubrication, and measure arch-end rotation at different temperatures to confirm the hinges still turn; monitor abutment horizontal and vertical movement by precise survey against historical records.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"支承鉸接應列為關鍵構件，訂定檢查週期、潤滑與防蝕程序，並以轉角與溫度的量測紀錄判斷是否仍有效；任何支承維修都要先評估施工期間的臨時荷載路徑並設停留點。","textEn":"Hinged bearings should be classed as critical components with set inspection intervals and lubrication and corrosion-protection procedures, judged effective by rotation-versus-temperature records; any bearing repair needs a prior assessment of the temporary load path and hold points.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons\"?","options":["定期檢查支承銷周圍有無腐蝕產物、磨耗痕跡與潤滑狀況，並量測拱端在不同溫度下的轉角，確認鉸接仍能轉動；橋台以精密測量監測水平與垂直位移，與歷史紀錄比較。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。"],"optionsEn":["Inspect around the bearing pins for corrosion products, wear marks and lubrication, and measure arch-end rotation at different temperatures to confirm the hinges still turn.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust."],"answer":0,"explanation":"定期檢查支承銷周圍有無腐蝕產物、磨耗痕跡與潤滑狀況，並量測拱端在不同溫度下的轉角，確認鉸接仍能轉動；橋台以精密測量監測水平與垂直位移，與歷史紀錄比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Inspect around the bearing pins for corrosion products, wear marks and lubrication, and measure arch-end rotation at different temperatures to confirm the hinges still turn; monitor abutment horizontal and vertical movement by precise survey against historical records. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b016-v13-16","title":"支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔：失效診斷","titleEn":"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「支承銷與橋台」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Bearing pins and abutments” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"支承銷卡滯時，雙鉸拱局部變成固定拱，溫度與活載在拱端產生原設計沒有考慮的彎矩，可能使端部桿件或接頭過應力；銷座腐蝕產生的膨脹也會改變接觸條件，造成應力集中。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"A seized pin turns the two-hinged arch locally into a fixed arch, so temperature and live load create end moments the original design never considered, possibly overstressing end members or joints; expanding corrosion in the seat alters contact and concentrates stress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：鉸接若因腐蝕或磨耗而卡住，拱的實際行為會偏離雙鉸假設，溫度變化在支點處產生額外彎矩。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: If corrosion or wear seizes a hinge, the arch departs from two-hinged behaviour and temperature changes induce extra moments at the supports.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"支承銷卡滯時，雙鉸拱局部變成固定拱，溫度與活載在拱端產生原設計沒有考慮的彎矩，可能使端部桿件或接頭過應力；銷座腐蝕產生的膨脹也會改變接觸條件，造成應力集中。","textEn":"A seized pin turns the two-hinged arch locally into a fixed arch, so temperature and live load create end moments the original design never considered, possibly overstressing end members or joints; expanding corrosion in the seat alters contact and concentrates stress.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「支承銷、橋台與非結構橋塔」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Bearing pins, abutments and pylons\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","支承銷卡滯時，雙鉸拱局部變成固定拱，溫度與活載在拱端產生原設計沒有考慮的彎矩，可能使端部桿件或接頭過應力；銷座腐蝕產生的膨脹也會改變接觸條件，造成應力集中。","鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","A seized pin turns the two-hinged arch locally into a fixed arch, so temperature and live load create end moments the original design never considered, possibly overstressing end members or joints.","A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"支承銷卡滯時，雙鉸拱局部變成固定拱，溫度與活載在拱端產生原設計沒有考慮的彎矩，可能使端部桿件或接頭過應力；銷座腐蝕產生的膨脹也會改變接觸條件，造成應力集中。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"A seized pin turns the two-hinged arch locally into a fixed arch, so temperature and live load create end moments the original design never considered, possibly overstressing end members or joints; expanding corrosion in the seat alters contact and concentrates stress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b016-v13-s3","title":"施工方法與施工階段控制","titleEn":"Construction methods and stage control","description":"本階段聚焦「懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索」與「1930 年拱頂合龍」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Cantilever erection with anchor cables\" and \"The 1930 crown closure\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b016-v13-17","title":"懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Cantilever erection with anchor cables: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-16"],"objective":"說明「隧道錨碇鋼索」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Tunnel-anchored cables” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雪梨港在架設時不能設置中間支架，兩個半拱只能從兩岸同時向港中央懸臂伸出。每個半拱在完成前都像一支從支承銷伸出的長懸臂，自重會讓它繞支承銷向港內傾倒；因此在兩岸岩盤中開挖 U 形隧道，以 128 條鋼索穿過隧道並連接到半拱上弦，把傾覆力矩拉回岸上。拱上各有一台爬升吊機沿著已完成的上弦向前移動，逐段吊裝新構件；隨著懸臂變長，鋼索拉力持續增加，必須依計算逐步調整。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「隧道錨碇鋼索」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"No intermediate falsework was possible in the harbour, so the two half-arches were cantilevered simultaneously from each shore toward the centre. Until completed, each half-arch acts like a long cantilever from its bearing pin, its weight trying to rotate it into the harbour; so U-shaped tunnels were cut into the rock on each shore and 128 steel cables passed through them and connected to the top chord of the half-arch, pulling the overturning moment back to shore. A creeper crane on each half moved forward along the completed top chord, lifting each new piece; as the cantilever grew, the cable pull increased and was adjusted step by step to calculation. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Tunnel-anchored cables” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以半拱接近完成時估算：半拱鋼重約 39,000/2 = 19,500 t，即約 191 MN；若重心距支承銷水平 110 m、錨索對支承銷的力臂 55 m，所需拉力 T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN，平均每條鋼索約 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Near completion, each half-arch weighs about 39,000/2 = 19,500 t, about 191 MN; with its centroid 110 m from the pin horizontally and a cable lever arm of 55 m about the pin, the required pull is T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN, about 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN per cable on average.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「隧道錨碇鋼索」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Tunnel-anchored cables”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-17-k1","title":"懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索","titleEn":"Cantilever erection with anchor cables","text":"雪梨港在架設時不能設置中間支架，兩個半拱只能從兩岸同時向港中央懸臂伸出。每個半拱在完成前都像一支從支承銷伸出的長懸臂，自重會讓它繞支承銷向港內傾倒；因此在兩岸岩盤中開挖 U 形隧道，以 128 條鋼索穿過隧道並連接到半拱上弦，把傾覆力矩拉回岸上。","textEn":"No intermediate falsework was possible in the harbour, so the two half-arches were cantilevered simultaneously from each shore toward the centre. Until completed, each half-arch acts like a long cantilever from its bearing pin, its weight trying to rotate it into the harbour; so U-shaped tunnels were cut into the rock on each shore and 128 steel cables passed through them and connected to the top chord of the half-arch, pulling the overturning moment back to shore.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Cantilever erection with anchor cables\" is correct?","options":["鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。","兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","雪梨港在架設時不能設置中間支架，兩個半拱只能從兩岸同時向港中央懸臂伸出。"],"optionsEn":["A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support.","The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","No intermediate falsework was possible in the harbour, so the two half-arches were cantilevered simultaneously from each shore toward the centre."],"answer":2,"explanation":"雪梨港在架設時不能設置中間支架，兩個半拱只能從兩岸同時向港中央懸臂伸出。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"No intermediate falsework was possible in the harbour, so the two half-arches were cantilevered simultaneously from each shore toward the centre. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b016-v13-18","title":"懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索：定量估算","titleEn":"Cantilever erection with anchor cables: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「隧道錨碇鋼索」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Tunnel-anchored cables” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以半拱接近完成時估算：半拱鋼重約 39,000/2 = 19,500 t，即約 191 MN；若重心距支承銷水平 110 m、錨索對支承銷的力臂 55 m，所需拉力 T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN，平均每條鋼索約 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN。重心與力臂為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Near completion, each half-arch weighs about 39,000/2 = 19,500 t, about 191 MN; with its centroid 110 m from the pin horizontally and a cable lever arm of 55 m about the pin, the required pull is T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN, about 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN per cable on average. Centroid and lever arm are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：每吊裝一段後量測半拱端點高程與平面位置，並量測代表性錨索的拉力，與施工階段計算比較；錨碇隧道的岩體與錨座在架設前做驗證試驗，確認能承受設計拉力並有餘裕。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: After each segment, survey the half-arch tip level and position and measure selected cable forces against staged calculations; before erection, proof-test the anchorage tunnels' rock and seats to confirm the design pull with margin.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以半拱接近完成時估算：半拱鋼重約 39,000/2 = 19,500 t，即約 191 MN；若重心距支承銷水平 110 m、錨索對支承銷的力臂 55 m，所需拉力 T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN，平均每條鋼索約 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN。重心與力臂為教學假設。","textEn":"Near completion, each half-arch weighs about 39,000/2 = 19,500 t, about 191 MN; with its centroid 110 m from the pin horizontally and a cable lever arm of 55 m about the pin, the required pull is T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN, about 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN per cable on average. Centroid and lever arm are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Cantilever erection with anchor cables\", which statement holds?","options":["以半拱接近完成時估算：半拱鋼重約 39,000/2 = 19,500 t，即約 191 MN。","百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。","遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。"],"optionsEn":["Near completion, each half-arch weighs about 39,000/2 = 19,500 t, about 191 MN.","A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems.","A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以半拱接近完成時估算：半拱鋼重約 39,000/2 = 19,500 t，即約 191 MN；若重心距支承銷水平 110 m、錨索對支承銷的力臂 55 m，所需拉力 T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN，平均每條鋼索約 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Near completion, each half-arch weighs about 39,000/2 = 19,500 t, about 191 MN; with its centroid 110 m from the pin horizontally and a cable lever arm of 55 m about the pin, the required pull is T = W·x/h = 191×110/55 ≈ 383 MN, about 383/128 ≈ 3.0 MN per cable on average. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b016-v13-19","title":"懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Cantilever erection with anchor cables: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「隧道錨碇鋼索」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Tunnel-anchored cables” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"每吊裝一段後量測半拱端點高程與平面位置，並量測代表性錨索的拉力，與施工階段計算比較；錨碇隧道的岩體與錨座在架設前做驗證試驗，確認能承受設計拉力並有餘裕。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"After each segment, survey the half-arch tip level and position and measure selected cable forces against staged calculations; before erection, proof-test the anchorage tunnels' rock and seats to confirm the design pull with margin. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：懸臂架設計畫應列出每個階段的錨索拉力、端點高程與允差，以及錨碇驗證試驗結果；每階段完成後由設計者與施工者共同確認量測值在允差內，才可進入下一段吊裝。","observationEn":"Site practice: The cantilever erection plan should list cable forces, tip levels and tolerances for each stage together with anchorage proof-test results; after each stage the designer and builder jointly confirm measurements within tolerance before the next lift.","failure":"注意干擾：若錨索拉力分配不均，某些鋼索超載而斷裂，半拱的傾覆平衡被打破；錨碇岩體若有未發現的弱面，隧道錨座在巨大拉力下滑動，懸臂端下沉並可能造成倒塌。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uneven cable force distribution can overload and break some cables, upsetting the half-arch's balance against overturning; an undetected weak plane in the anchorage rock can let the tunnel seat slide under the huge pull, dropping the cantilever tip and risking collapse. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"每吊裝一段後量測半拱端點高程與平面位置，並量測代表性錨索的拉力，與施工階段計算比較；錨碇隧道的岩體與錨座在架設前做驗證試驗，確認能承受設計拉力並有餘裕。","textEn":"After each segment, survey the half-arch tip level and position and measure selected cable forces against staged calculations; before erection, proof-test the anchorage tunnels' rock and seats to confirm the design pull with margin.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"懸臂架設計畫應列出每個階段的錨索拉力、端點高程與允差，以及錨碇驗證試驗結果；每階段完成後由設計者與施工者共同確認量測值在允差內，才可進入下一段吊裝。","textEn":"The cantilever erection plan should list cable forces, tip levels and tolerances for each stage together with anchorage proof-test results; after each stage the designer and builder jointly confirm measurements within tolerance before the next lift.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Cantilever erection with anchor cables\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","每吊裝一段後量測半拱端點高程與平面位置，並量測代表性錨索的拉力，與施工階段計算比較；錨碇隧道的岩體與錨座在架設前做驗證試驗，確認能承受設計拉力並有餘裕。","拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","After each segment, survey the half-arch tip level and position and measure selected cable forces against staged calculations.","An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每吊裝一段後量測半拱端點高程與平面位置，並量測代表性錨索的拉力，與施工階段計算比較；錨碇隧道的岩體與錨座在架設前做驗證試驗，確認能承受設計拉力並有餘裕。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"After each segment, survey the half-arch tip level and position and measure selected cable forces against staged calculations; before erection, proof-test the anchorage tunnels' rock and seats to confirm the design pull with margin. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b016-v13-20","title":"懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索：失效診斷","titleEn":"Cantilever erection with anchor cables: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「隧道錨碇鋼索」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Tunnel-anchored cables” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若錨索拉力分配不均，某些鋼索超載而斷裂，半拱的傾覆平衡被打破；錨碇岩體若有未發現的弱面，隧道錨座在巨大拉力下滑動，懸臂端下沉並可能造成倒塌。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uneven cable force distribution can overload and break some cables, upsetting the half-arch's balance against overturning; an undetected weak plane in the anchorage rock can let the tunnel seat slide under the huge pull, dropping the cantilever tip and risking collapse. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：拱上各有一台爬升吊機沿著已完成的上弦向前移動，逐段吊裝新構件；隨著懸臂變長，鋼索拉力持續增加，必須依計算逐步調整。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: A creeper crane on each half moved forward along the completed top chord, lifting each new piece; as the cantilever grew, the cable pull increased and was adjusted step by step to calculation.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若錨索拉力分配不均，某些鋼索超載而斷裂，半拱的傾覆平衡被打破；錨碇岩體若有未發現的弱面，隧道錨座在巨大拉力下滑動，懸臂端下沉並可能造成倒塌。","textEn":"Uneven cable force distribution can overload and break some cables, upsetting the half-arch's balance against overturning; an undetected weak plane in the anchorage rock can let the tunnel seat slide under the huge pull, dropping the cantilever tip and risking collapse.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「懸臂架設與錨碇鋼索」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Cantilever erection with anchor cables\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","若錨索拉力分配不均，某些鋼索超載而斷裂，半拱的傾覆平衡被打破；錨碇岩體若有未發現的弱面，隧道錨座在巨大拉力下滑動，懸臂端下沉並可能造成倒塌。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","Uneven cable force distribution can overload and break some cables, upsetting the half-arch's balance against overturning."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若錨索拉力分配不均，某些鋼索超載而斷裂，半拱的傾覆平衡被打破；錨碇岩體若有未發現的弱面，隧道錨座在巨大拉力下滑動，懸臂端下沉並可能造成倒塌。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uneven cable force distribution can overload and break some cables, upsetting the half-arch's balance against overturning; an undetected weak plane in the anchorage rock can let the tunnel seat slide under the huge pull, dropping the cantilever tip and risking collapse. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b016-v13-21","title":"1930 年拱頂合龍：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The 1930 crown closure: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-20"],"objective":"說明「拱頂合龍」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Crown closure” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"兩個半拱伸到港中央時，端點之間預留一段間隙，接著以逐步放鬆錨索的方式讓兩個半拱繞支承銷向內、向下轉動，直到在拱頂相接；公開資料指出兩個半拱在 1930 年 8 月 19 日首次接合，鉚接完成後拱即可自我支撐，錨索隨後拆除。合龍時間對溫度非常敏感：白天日照使鋼材膨脹、間隙縮小，夜間冷卻又使間隙擴大，因此放索與接合必須配合溫度變化，確保接合時兩端的位置、角度與內力都符合設計。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「拱頂合龍」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"When the half-arches reached mid-harbour, a gap was left between their tips, and the cables were then slackened step by step so each half rotated inward and downward about its pin until they met at the crown; public sources record that the halves first met on 19 August 1930, after which riveting made the arch self-supporting and the cables were removed. Closure is highly temperature-sensitive: sun expands the steel and narrows the gap by day, and cooling widens it at night, so cable release and connection had to follow temperature to ensure position, angle and internal forces at the joint matched design. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Crown closure” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：放鬆錨索 Δc = 0.10 m、力臂 h = 57 m，半拱繞支承銷轉角 θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Letting out the cables by Δc = 0.10 m on a lever arm of h = 57 m rotates the half-arch about its pin by θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad.","failure":"常見誤解：「兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「拱頂合龍」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Crown closure”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-21-k1","title":"1930 年拱頂合龍","titleEn":"The 1930 crown closure","text":"兩個半拱伸到港中央時，端點之間預留一段間隙，接著以逐步放鬆錨索的方式讓兩個半拱繞支承銷向內、向下轉動，直到在拱頂相接；公開資料指出兩個半拱在 1930 年 8 月 19 日首次接合，鉚接完成後拱即可自我支撐，錨索隨後拆除。合龍時間對溫度非常敏感：白天日照使鋼材膨脹、間隙縮小，夜間冷卻又使間隙擴大，因此放索與接合必須配合溫度變化，確保接合時兩端的位置、角度與內力都符合設計。","textEn":"When the half-arches reached mid-harbour, a gap was left between their tips, and the cables were then slackened step by step so each half rotated inward and downward about its pin until they met at the crown; public sources record that the halves first met on 19 August 1930, after which riveting made the arch self-supporting and the cables were removed. Closure is highly temperature-sensitive: sun expands the steel and narrows the gap by day, and cooling widens it at night, so cable release and connection had to follow temperature to ensure position, angle and internal forces at the joint matched design.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1930 年拱頂合龍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The 1930 crown closure\" is correct?","options":["兩個半拱伸到港中央時，端點之間預留一段間隙，接著以逐步放鬆錨索的方式讓兩個半拱繞支承銷向內、向下轉動，直到在拱頂相接。","兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。"],"optionsEn":["When the half-arches reached mid-harbour, a gap was left between their tips, and the cables were then slackened step by step so each half rotated inward and downward about its pin until they met at the crown.","The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩個半拱伸到港中央時，端點之間預留一段間隙，接著以逐步放鬆錨索的方式讓兩個半拱繞支承銷向內、向下轉動，直到在拱頂相接；公開資料指出兩個半拱在 1930 年 8 月 19 日首次接合，鉚接完成後拱即可自我支撐，錨索隨後拆除。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"When the half-arches reached mid-harbour, a gap was left between their tips, and the cables were then slackened step by step so each half rotated inward and downward about its pin until they met at the crown; public sources record that the halves first met on 19 August 1930, after which riveting made the arch self-supporting and the cables were removed. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b016-v13-22","title":"1930 年拱頂合龍：定量估算","titleEn":"The 1930 crown closure: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「拱頂合龍」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Crown closure” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：放鬆錨索 Δc = 0.10 m、力臂 h = 57 m，半拱繞支承銷轉角 θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad。若拱頂端點距支承銷水平 251.5 m、高 120 m，端點向內移動約 θ×120 ≈ 0.21 m，向下約 θ×251.5 ≈ 0.44 m。半拱弧長約 290 m，溫度變化 10 °C 時長度改變 290×1.2×10⁻⁵×10 ≈ 35 mm。幾何為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Letting out the cables by Δc = 0.10 m on a lever arm of h = 57 m rotates the half-arch about its pin by θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad. With the tip 251.5 m from the pin horizontally and 120 m above it, the tip moves inward by about θ×120 ≈ 0.21 m and down by about θ×251.5 ≈ 0.44 m. A half-arch about 290 m long changes length by 290×1.2×10⁻⁵×10 ≈ 35 mm for a 10 °C change. Geometry is a teaching assumption. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：合龍前持續量測兩端間隙、高程與鋼溫，建立間隙與溫度、放索量的關係；接合後量測拱頂高程與拱軸線形，確認拱已承載自重並記錄錨索卸載過程中的拉力變化，與設計預測比較。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before closure measure the gap, levels and steel temperature continuously, building the relation of gap to temperature and cable release; after connection survey crown level and arch axis to confirm the arch carries its own weight, and record cable forces as they unload for comparison with predictions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"放鬆錨索 Δc = 0.10 m、力臂 h = 57 m，半拱繞支承銷轉角 θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad。若拱頂端點距支承銷水平 251.5 m、高 120 m，端點向內移動約 θ×120 ≈ 0.21 m，向下約 θ×251.5 ≈ 0.44 m。半拱弧長約 290 m，溫度變化 10 °C 時長度改變 290×1.2×10⁻⁵×10 ≈ 35 mm。幾何為教學假設。","textEn":"Letting out the cables by Δc = 0.10 m on a lever arm of h = 57 m rotates the half-arch about its pin by θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad. With the tip 251.5 m from the pin horizontally and 120 m above it, the tip moves inward by about θ×120 ≈ 0.21 m and down by about θ×251.5 ≈ 0.44 m. A half-arch about 290 m long changes length by 290×1.2×10⁻⁵×10 ≈ 35 mm for a 10 °C change. Geometry is a teaching assumption.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「1930 年拱頂合龍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The 1930 crown closure\", which statement holds?","options":["鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。","放鬆錨索 Δc = 0.10 m、力臂 h = 57 m，半拱繞支承銷轉角 θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad。","雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。"],"optionsEn":["As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.","Letting out the cables by Δc = 0.10 m on a lever arm of h = 57 m rotates the half-arch about its pin by θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad.","The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust."],"answer":1,"explanation":"放鬆錨索 Δc = 0.10 m、力臂 h = 57 m，半拱繞支承銷轉角 θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Letting out the cables by Δc = 0.10 m on a lever arm of h = 57 m rotates the half-arch about its pin by θ = Δc/h ≈ 1.75 mrad. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b016-v13-23","title":"1930 年拱頂合龍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The 1930 crown closure: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「拱頂合龍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Crown closure” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"合龍前持續量測兩端間隙、高程與鋼溫，建立間隙與溫度、放索量的關係；接合後量測拱頂高程與拱軸線形，確認拱已承載自重並記錄錨索卸載過程中的拉力變化，與設計預測比較。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before closure measure the gap, levels and steel temperature continuously, building the relation of gap to temperature and cable release; after connection survey crown level and arch axis to confirm the arch carries its own weight, and record cable forces as they unload for comparison with predictions. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：合龍程序應明訂放索順序與每步量測、可接合的溫度與間隙範圍、臨時固定方式與接合後的錨索卸載步驟；每一步由設計方代表簽認，量測與溫度紀錄完整歸檔。","observationEn":"Site practice: The closure procedure should specify the cable-release sequence with measurements at each step, the temperature and gap range for connection, temporary fixing and the post-connection cable unloading steps; each step is signed by the designer's representative and all measurements and temperatures are archived.","failure":"注意干擾：若兩端在溫度快速變化時強行接合，接頭鉚接後鎖入額外的內力；兩端高程差或角度差未修正就接合，拱軸偏離設計，造成永久的附加彎矩與局部過應力。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Forcing the connection during rapid temperature change locks extra forces into the riveted joint; connecting with uncorrected level or angle differences shifts the arch axis from design, leaving permanent additional bending and local overstress. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"合龍前持續量測兩端間隙、高程與鋼溫，建立間隙與溫度、放索量的關係；接合後量測拱頂高程與拱軸線形，確認拱已承載自重並記錄錨索卸載過程中的拉力變化，與設計預測比較。","textEn":"Before closure measure the gap, levels and steel temperature continuously, building the relation of gap to temperature and cable release; after connection survey crown level and arch axis to confirm the arch carries its own weight, and record cable forces as they unload for comparison with predictions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"合龍程序應明訂放索順序與每步量測、可接合的溫度與間隙範圍、臨時固定方式與接合後的錨索卸載步驟；每一步由設計方代表簽認，量測與溫度紀錄完整歸檔。","textEn":"The closure procedure should specify the cable-release sequence with measurements at each step, the temperature and gap range for connection, temporary fixing and the post-connection cable unloading steps; each step is signed by the designer's representative and all measurements and temperatures are archived.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「1930 年拱頂合龍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The 1930 crown closure\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。","合龍前持續量測兩端間隙、高程與鋼溫，建立間隙與溫度、放索量的關係；接合後量測拱頂高程與拱軸線形，確認拱已承載自重並記錄錨索卸載過程中的拉力變化，與設計預測比較。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.","Before closure measure the gap, levels and steel temperature continuously, building the relation of gap to temperature and cable release."],"answer":2,"explanation":"合龍前持續量測兩端間隙、高程與鋼溫，建立間隙與溫度、放索量的關係；接合後量測拱頂高程與拱軸線形，確認拱已承載自重並記錄錨索卸載過程中的拉力變化，與設計預測比較。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before closure measure the gap, levels and steel temperature continuously, building the relation of gap to temperature and cable release; after connection survey crown level and arch axis to confirm the arch carries its own weight, and record cable forces as they unload for comparison with predictions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b016-v13-24","title":"1930 年拱頂合龍：失效診斷","titleEn":"The 1930 crown closure: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「拱頂合龍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Crown closure” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若兩端在溫度快速變化時強行接合，接頭鉚接後鎖入額外的內力；兩端高程差或角度差未修正就接合，拱軸偏離設計，造成永久的附加彎矩與局部過應力。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Forcing the connection during rapid temperature change locks extra forces into the riveted joint; connecting with uncorrected level or angle differences shifts the arch axis from design, leaving permanent additional bending and local overstress. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：合龍時間對溫度非常敏感：白天日照使鋼材膨脹、間隙縮小，夜間冷卻又使間隙擴大，因此放索與接合必須配合溫度變化，確保接合時兩端的位置、角度與內力都符合設計。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Closure is highly temperature-sensitive: sun expands the steel and narrows the gap by day, and cooling widens it at night, so cable release and connection had to follow temperature to ensure position, angle and internal forces at the joint matched design.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若兩端在溫度快速變化時強行接合，接頭鉚接後鎖入額外的內力；兩端高程差或角度差未修正就接合，拱軸偏離設計，造成永久的附加彎矩與局部過應力。","textEn":"Forcing the connection during rapid temperature change locks extra forces into the riveted joint; connecting with uncorrected level or angle differences shifts the arch axis from design, leaving permanent additional bending and local overstress.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「1930 年拱頂合龍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The 1930 crown closure\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["若兩端在溫度快速變化時強行接合，接頭鉚接後鎖入額外的內力；兩端高程差或角度差未修正就接合，拱軸偏離設計，造成永久的附加彎矩與局部過應力。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。"],"optionsEn":["Forcing the connection during rapid temperature change locks extra forces into the riveted joint.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"若兩端在溫度快速變化時強行接合，接頭鉚接後鎖入額外的內力；兩端高程差或角度差未修正就接合，拱軸偏離設計，造成永久的附加彎矩與局部過應力。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Forcing the connection during rapid temperature change locks extra forces into the riveted joint; connecting with uncorrected level or angle differences shifts the arch axis from design, leaving permanent additional bending and local overstress. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b016-v13-s4","title":"試驗、量測與監測驗證","titleEn":"Testing, measurement and monitoring","description":"本階段聚焦「1932 年機車載重試驗」與「現代交通下的疲勞評估」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"The 1932 locomotive load test\" and \"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b016-v13-25","title":"1932 年機車載重試驗：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"The 1932 locomotive load test: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-24"],"objective":"說明「機車載重試驗」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Locomotive load test” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大橋通車前於 1932 年初進行載重試驗，公開資料記載最多以 96 輛蒸汽機車在四條鐵路軌道上首尾相接排列，試驗持續數週。這種試驗的目的不是證明極限強度，而是以已知的大荷載檢查結構反應是否與計算一致：撓度、拱頂下沉、支承轉動與桿件應變都應呈線性並在卸載後回復。以機車作為試驗荷載有兩個優點：重量可以精確掌握，而且可以依需要排列在半跨或全跨，模擬最不利的鐵路載重。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「機車載重試驗」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Before opening, a load test in early 1932 placed up to 96 steam locomotives end to end on the four rail tracks, according to public records, over several weeks. Its purpose was not to prove ultimate strength but to use a large known load to check that structural response agreed with calculation: deflections, crown settlement, support rotation and member strains should be linear and recover on unloading. Locomotives made good test loads for two reasons: their weights were precisely known, and they could be arranged on half or full spans to imitate the most unfavourable rail loading. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Locomotive load test” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：假設每輛機車含煤水車重 120 t、長 20 m：96 輛共 96×120 = 11,520 t。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Assume each locomotive with tender weighs 120 t and is 20 m long: 96 of them total 96×120 = 11,520 t.","failure":"常見誤解：「載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「機車載重試驗」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Locomotive load test”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-25-k1","title":"1932 年機車載重試驗","titleEn":"The 1932 locomotive load test","text":"大橋通車前於 1932 年初進行載重試驗，公開資料記載最多以 96 輛蒸汽機車在四條鐵路軌道上首尾相接排列，試驗持續數週。這種試驗的目的不是證明極限強度，而是以已知的大荷載檢查結構反應是否與計算一致：撓度、拱頂下沉、支承轉動與桿件應變都應呈線性並在卸載後回復。","textEn":"Before opening, a load test in early 1932 placed up to 96 steam locomotives end to end on the four rail tracks, according to public records, over several weeks. Its purpose was not to prove ultimate strength but to use a large known load to check that structural response agreed with calculation: deflections, crown settlement, support rotation and member strains should be linear and recover on unloading.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「1932 年機車載重試驗」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"The 1932 locomotive load test\" is correct?","options":["載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。","大橋通車前於 1932 年初進行載重試驗，公開資料記載最多以 96 輛蒸汽機車在四條鐵路軌道上首尾相接排列，試驗持續數週。","百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。"],"optionsEn":["A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough.","Before opening, a load test in early 1932 placed up to 96 steam locomotives end to end on the four rail tracks, according to public records, over several weeks.","A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大橋通車前於 1932 年初進行載重試驗，公開資料記載最多以 96 輛蒸汽機車在四條鐵路軌道上首尾相接排列，試驗持續數週。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Before opening, a load test in early 1932 placed up to 96 steam locomotives end to end on the four rail tracks, according to public records, over several weeks. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b016-v13-26","title":"1932 年機車載重試驗：定量估算","titleEn":"The 1932 locomotive load test: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「機車載重試驗」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Locomotive load test” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：假設每輛機車含煤水車重 120 t、長 20 m：96 輛共 96×120 = 11,520 t。單一軌道的線荷載約 120×9.81/20 ≈ 58.9 kN/m，四條軌道同時排滿約 235 kN/m。機車重量與長度為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Assume each locomotive with tender weighs 120 t and is 20 m long: 96 of them total 96×120 = 11,520 t. One track then carries about 120×9.81/20 ≈ 58.9 kN/m, and four full tracks about 235 kN/m. Locomotive mass and length are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：依計算預先列出各荷載排列下拱頂與四分點的預期撓度，試驗時以水準儀量測並記錄氣溫；比較實測與預測的比值，並確認卸載後殘餘變形很小。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: List expected crown and quarter-point deflections for each arrangement in advance, measure them by levelling during the test while recording air temperature, compare measured-to-predicted ratios and confirm small residual deformation after unloading.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"假設每輛機車含煤水車重 120 t、長 20 m：96 輛共 96×120 = 11,520 t。單一軌道的線荷載約 120×9.81/20 ≈ 58.9 kN/m，四條軌道同時排滿約 235 kN/m。機車重量與長度為教學假設。","textEn":"Assume each locomotive with tender weighs 120 t and is 20 m long: 96 of them total 96×120 = 11,520 t. One track then carries about 120×9.81/20 ≈ 58.9 kN/m, and four full tracks about 235 kN/m. Locomotive mass and length are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「1932 年機車載重試驗」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"The 1932 locomotive load test\", which statement holds?","options":["遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。","拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。","假設每輛機車含煤水車重 120 t、長 20 m：96 輛共 96×120 = 11,520 t。"],"optionsEn":["A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value.","An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered.","Assume each locomotive with tender weighs 120 t and is 20 m long: 96 of them total 96×120 = 11,520 t."],"answer":2,"explanation":"假設每輛機車含煤水車重 120 t、長 20 m：96 輛共 96×120 = 11,520 t。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Assume each locomotive with tender weighs 120 t and is 20 m long: 96 of them total 96×120 = 11,520 t. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b016-v13-27","title":"1932 年機車載重試驗：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"The 1932 locomotive load test: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「機車載重試驗」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Locomotive load test” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"依計算預先列出各荷載排列下拱頂與四分點的預期撓度，試驗時以水準儀量測並記錄氣溫；比較實測與預測的比值，並確認卸載後殘餘變形很小。今日類似試驗會加上應變計與位移計，以自動化記錄取代人工讀數。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"List expected crown and quarter-point deflections for each arrangement in advance, measure them by levelling during the test while recording air temperature, compare measured-to-predicted ratios and confirm small residual deformation after unloading. A similar test today would add strain gauges and displacement transducers with automatic logging instead of manual readings. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：任何載重試驗都應事先公開荷載排列、預期反應、停止條件與允收準則，試驗荷載不超過設計使用荷載的規定比例；結果與原始紀錄一起永久保存，成為日後評估的基準。","observationEn":"Site practice: Any load test should publish load arrangements, expected responses, stop criteria and acceptance criteria in advance, keeping the test load within a specified fraction of design service load; results are archived permanently with raw records as the baseline for later assessments.","failure":"注意干擾：若試驗期間溫度變化大而未修正，拱的熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，讓實測值看似異常；機車排列若不對稱且未事先分析，局部桿件或吊桿可能承受超過設計的荷載。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Large temperature changes during the test without correction can produce thermal movements as large as the load deflection, making measurements look abnormal; asymmetric locomotive arrangements not analysed beforehand can overload individual members or hangers. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"依計算預先列出各荷載排列下拱頂與四分點的預期撓度，試驗時以水準儀量測並記錄氣溫；比較實測與預測的比值，並確認卸載後殘餘變形很小。今日類似試驗會加上應變計與位移計，以自動化記錄取代人工讀數。","textEn":"List expected crown and quarter-point deflections for each arrangement in advance, measure them by levelling during the test while recording air temperature, compare measured-to-predicted ratios and confirm small residual deformation after unloading. A similar test today would add strain gauges and displacement transducers with automatic logging instead of manual readings.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"任何載重試驗都應事先公開荷載排列、預期反應、停止條件與允收準則，試驗荷載不超過設計使用荷載的規定比例；結果與原始紀錄一起永久保存，成為日後評估的基準。","textEn":"Any load test should publish load arrangements, expected responses, stop criteria and acceptance criteria in advance, keeping the test load within a specified fraction of design service load; results are archived permanently with raw records as the baseline for later assessments.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「1932 年機車載重試驗」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"The 1932 locomotive load test\"?","options":["依計算預先列出各荷載排列下拱頂與四分點的預期撓度，試驗時以水準儀量測並記錄氣溫；比較實測與預測的比值，並確認卸載後殘餘變形很小。","量測時不必記錄溫度、日照、風與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["List expected crown and quarter-point deflections for each arrangement in advance, measure them by levelling during the test while recording air temperature, compare measured-to-predicted ratios and confirm small residual deformation after unloading.","Temperature, sunshine, wind and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依計算預先列出各荷載排列下拱頂與四分點的預期撓度，試驗時以水準儀量測並記錄氣溫；比較實測與預測的比值，並確認卸載後殘餘變形很小。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"List expected crown and quarter-point deflections for each arrangement in advance, measure them by levelling during the test while recording air temperature, compare measured-to-predicted ratios and confirm small residual deformation after unloading. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b016-v13-28","title":"1932 年機車載重試驗：失效診斷","titleEn":"The 1932 locomotive load test: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「機車載重試驗」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Locomotive load test” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若試驗期間溫度變化大而未修正，拱的熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，讓實測值看似異常；機車排列若不對稱且未事先分析，局部桿件或吊桿可能承受超過設計的荷載。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Large temperature changes during the test without correction can produce thermal movements as large as the load deflection, making measurements look abnormal; asymmetric locomotive arrangements not analysed beforehand can overload individual members or hangers. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：以機車作為試驗荷載有兩個優點：重量可以精確掌握，而且可以依需要排列在半跨或全跨，模擬最不利的鐵路載重。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Locomotives made good test loads for two reasons: their weights were precisely known, and they could be arranged on half or full spans to imitate the most unfavourable rail loading.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若試驗期間溫度變化大而未修正，拱的熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，讓實測值看似異常；機車排列若不對稱且未事先分析，局部桿件或吊桿可能承受超過設計的荷載。","textEn":"Large temperature changes during the test without correction can produce thermal movements as large as the load deflection, making measurements look abnormal; asymmetric locomotive arrangements not analysed beforehand can overload individual members or hangers.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「1932 年機車載重試驗」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"The 1932 locomotive load test\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","若試驗期間溫度變化大而未修正，拱的熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，讓實測值看似異常；機車排列若不對稱且未事先分析，局部桿件或吊桿可能承受超過設計的荷載。","百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Large temperature changes during the test without correction can produce thermal movements as large as the load deflection, making measurements look abnormal.","A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若試驗期間溫度變化大而未修正，拱的熱變形可能與載重撓度同量級，讓實測值看似異常；機車排列若不對稱且未事先分析，局部桿件或吊桿可能承受超過設計的荷載。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Large temperature changes during the test without correction can produce thermal movements as large as the load deflection, making measurements look abnormal; asymmetric locomotive arrangements not analysed beforehand can overload individual members or hangers. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b016-v13-29","title":"現代交通下的疲勞評估：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-28"],"objective":"說明「鉚接細節疲勞評估」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大橋設計於 1920 年代，當時的交通量與今日完全不同：公開資料指出 2017 年每日有逾 200 班列車、約 16 萬輛車通過。每一列車或重車通過都在吊桿、橫梁與鐵路縱梁產生應力循環，百年累積的循環次數遠超原設計的想像。鉚接細節的疲勞強度一般歸類為較低的類別，而鉚釘孔、腐蝕坑與鬆動的鉚釘都會降低壽命。因此現代評估會以實測應力與交通資料計算累積損傷，找出最需要檢查與補強的細節。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「鉚接細節疲勞評估」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The bridge was designed in the 1920s for traffic utterly different from today's: public sources cite more than 200 trains and about 160,000 vehicles a day in 2017. Every train or heavy vehicle produces stress cycles in hangers, cross-girders and rail stringers, and a century of accumulation far exceeds anything the original designers imagined. Riveted details usually fall into a lower fatigue category, and rivet holes, corrosion pits and loose rivets reduce life further. Modern assessment therefore computes cumulative damage from measured stresses and traffic data to find the details that most need inspection and strengthening. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 AASHTO 疲勞類別 D（常用於鉚接細節）為例：N = A/Δσ³，A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Using AASHTO fatigue category D, common for riveted details: N = A/Δσ³ with A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³.","failure":"常見誤解：「百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「鉚接細節疲勞評估」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-29-k1","title":"現代交通下的疲勞評估","titleEn":"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic","text":"大橋設計於 1920 年代，當時的交通量與今日完全不同：公開資料指出 2017 年每日有逾 200 班列車、約 16 萬輛車通過。每一列車或重車通過都在吊桿、橫梁與鐵路縱梁產生應力循環，百年累積的循環次數遠超原設計的想像。","textEn":"The bridge was designed in the 1920s for traffic utterly different from today's: public sources cite more than 200 trains and about 160,000 vehicles a day in 2017. Every train or heavy vehicle produces stress cycles in hangers, cross-girders and rail stringers, and a century of accumulation far exceeds anything the original designers imagined.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「現代交通下的疲勞評估」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic\" is correct?","options":["百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。","鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。","大橋設計於 1920 年代，當時的交通量與今日完全不同：公開資料指出 2017 年每日有逾 200 班列車、約 16 萬輛車通過。"],"optionsEn":["A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems.","As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.","The bridge was designed in the 1920s for traffic utterly different from today's: public sources cite more than 200 trains and about 160,000 vehicles a day in 2017."],"answer":2,"explanation":"大橋設計於 1920 年代，當時的交通量與今日完全不同：公開資料指出 2017 年每日有逾 200 班列車、約 16 萬輛車通過。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The bridge was designed in the 1920s for traffic utterly different from today's: public sources cite more than 200 trains and about 160,000 vehicles a day in 2017. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b016-v13-30","title":"現代交通下的疲勞評估：定量估算","titleEn":"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「鉚接細節疲勞評估」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 AASHTO 疲勞類別 D（常用於鉚接細節）為例：N = A/Δσ³，A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³。等效應力幅 Δσ = 30 MPa 時 N ≈ 7.08×10¹¹/27,000 ≈ 2.62×10⁷ 次；若每日 500 次有效循環，約 2.62×10⁷/(500×365) ≈ 144 年。循環數與應力幅為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Using AASHTO fatigue category D, common for riveted details: N = A/Δσ³ with A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³. At an equivalent range Δσ = 30 MPa, N ≈ 7.08×10¹¹/27,000 ≈ 2.62×10⁷ cycles; at 500 effective cycles a day that is about 2.62×10⁷/(500×365) ≈ 144 years. Cycle count and stress range are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：在代表性吊桿、橫梁與縱梁裝設應變計，記錄數週的列車與車流應力歷時，以雨流計數求等效應力幅與每日循環數；結合歷史交通資料估算已累積的損傷，並以目視、磁粒或渦電流檢測高風險細節。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Fit strain gauges to representative hangers, cross-girders and stringers, record weeks of train and traffic stress histories, and derive equivalent ranges and daily cycles by rainflow counting; estimate accumulated damage with historical traffic data, and inspect high-risk details by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 AASHTO 疲勞類別 D（常用於鉚接細節）為例：N = A/Δσ³，A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³。等效應力幅 Δσ = 30 MPa 時 N ≈ 7.08×10¹¹/27,000 ≈ 2.62×10⁷ 次；若每日 500 次有效循環，約 2.62×10⁷/(500×365) ≈ 144 年。循環數與應力幅為教學假設。","textEn":"Using AASHTO fatigue category D, common for riveted details: N = A/Δσ³ with A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³. At an equivalent range Δσ = 30 MPa, N ≈ 7.08×10¹¹/27,000 ≈ 2.62×10⁷ cycles; at 500 effective cycles a day that is about 2.62×10⁷/(500×365) ≈ 144 years. Cycle count and stress range are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「現代交通下的疲勞評估」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic\", which statement holds?","options":["以 AASHTO 疲勞類別 D（常用於鉚接細節）為例：N = A/Δσ³，A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³。","雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。","鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。"],"optionsEn":["Using AASHTO fatigue category D, common for riveted details: N = A/Δσ³ with A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³.","The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust.","Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以 AASHTO 疲勞類別 D（常用於鉚接細節）為例：N = A/Δσ³，A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Using AASHTO fatigue category D, common for riveted details: N = A/Δσ³ with A = 21.6×10⁸ ksi³ ≈ 7.08×10¹¹ MPa³. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b016-v13-31","title":"現代交通下的疲勞評估：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「鉚接細節疲勞評估」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"在代表性吊桿、橫梁與縱梁裝設應變計，記錄數週的列車與車流應力歷時，以雨流計數求等效應力幅與每日循環數；結合歷史交通資料估算已累積的損傷，並以目視、磁粒或渦電流檢測高風險細節。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Fit strain gauges to representative hangers, cross-girders and stringers, record weeks of train and traffic stress histories, and derive equivalent ranges and daily cycles by rainflow counting; estimate accumulated damage with historical traffic data, and inspect high-risk details by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：評估報告應依實測應力與交通量排定細節的檢查優先順序，對高風險細節縮短檢查週期；重大改變交通（例如新增重型列車或車道配置改變）前，必須重新評估疲勞。","observationEn":"Site practice: The assessment should rank details for inspection using measured stresses and traffic, shortening intervals for high-risk ones; before major traffic changes, such as heavier trains or new lane layouts, fatigue must be reassessed.","failure":"注意干擾：若只以設計時的交通量評估，歷史累積損傷被低估，疲勞裂紋可能在鉚釘孔邊緣萌生並在構件內擴展而未被發現；腐蝕與疲勞交互作用時，裂紋成長速度更快。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Assessing with design-era traffic underestimates accumulated damage, so fatigue cracks may start at rivet-hole edges and grow undetected; where corrosion and fatigue interact, cracks grow faster still. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"在代表性吊桿、橫梁與縱梁裝設應變計，記錄數週的列車與車流應力歷時，以雨流計數求等效應力幅與每日循環數；結合歷史交通資料估算已累積的損傷，並以目視、磁粒或渦電流檢測高風險細節。","textEn":"Fit strain gauges to representative hangers, cross-girders and stringers, record weeks of train and traffic stress histories, and derive equivalent ranges and daily cycles by rainflow counting; estimate accumulated damage with historical traffic data, and inspect high-risk details by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"評估報告應依實測應力與交通量排定細節的檢查優先順序，對高風險細節縮短檢查週期；重大改變交通（例如新增重型列車或車道配置改變）前，必須重新評估疲勞。","textEn":"The assessment should rank details for inspection using measured stresses and traffic, shortening intervals for high-risk ones; before major traffic changes, such as heavier trains or new lane layouts, fatigue must be reassessed.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「現代交通下的疲勞評估」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic\"?","options":["沿用另一座橋或另一棟建築的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","在代表性吊桿、橫梁與縱梁裝設應變計，記錄數週的列車與車流應力歷時，以雨流計數求等效應力幅與每日循環數。","鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another bridge or building counts as verifying this structure.","Fit strain gauges to representative hangers, cross-girders and stringers, record weeks of train and traffic stress histories, and derive equivalent ranges and daily cycles by rainflow counting.","A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support."],"answer":1,"explanation":"在代表性吊桿、橫梁與縱梁裝設應變計，記錄數週的列車與車流應力歷時，以雨流計數求等效應力幅與每日循環數；結合歷史交通資料估算已累積的損傷，並以目視、磁粒或渦電流檢測高風險細節。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Fit strain gauges to representative hangers, cross-girders and stringers, record weeks of train and traffic stress histories, and derive equivalent ranges and daily cycles by rainflow counting; estimate accumulated damage with historical traffic data, and inspect high-risk details by visual, magnetic-particle or eddy-current testing. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b016-v13-32","title":"現代交通下的疲勞評估：失效診斷","titleEn":"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「鉚接細節疲勞評估」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Riveted-detail fatigue assessment” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若只以設計時的交通量評估，歷史累積損傷被低估，疲勞裂紋可能在鉚釘孔邊緣萌生並在構件內擴展而未被發現；腐蝕與疲勞交互作用時，裂紋成長速度更快。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Assessing with design-era traffic underestimates accumulated damage, so fatigue cracks may start at rivet-hole edges and grow undetected; where corrosion and fatigue interact, cracks grow faster still. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：因此現代評估會以實測應力與交通資料計算累積損傷，找出最需要檢查與補強的細節。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Modern assessment therefore computes cumulative damage from measured stresses and traffic data to find the details that most need inspection and strengthening.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「百年老橋沒有倒，代表它不會有疲勞問題。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A century-old bridge that is still standing cannot have fatigue problems.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若只以設計時的交通量評估，歷史累積損傷被低估，疲勞裂紋可能在鉚釘孔邊緣萌生並在構件內擴展而未被發現；腐蝕與疲勞交互作用時，裂紋成長速度更快。","textEn":"Assessing with design-era traffic underestimates accumulated damage, so fatigue cracks may start at rivet-hole edges and grow undetected; where corrosion and fatigue interact, cracks grow faster still.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「現代交通下的疲勞評估」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Fatigue assessment under modern traffic\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。","若只以設計時的交通量評估，歷史累積損傷被低估，疲勞裂紋可能在鉚釘孔邊緣萌生並在構件內擴展而未被發現；腐蝕與疲勞交互作用時，裂紋成長速度更快。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.","Assessing with design-era traffic underestimates accumulated damage, so fatigue cracks may start at rivet-hole edges and grow undetected."],"answer":2,"explanation":"若只以設計時的交通量評估，歷史累積損傷被低估，疲勞裂紋可能在鉚釘孔邊緣萌生並在構件內擴展而未被發現；腐蝕與疲勞交互作用時，裂紋成長速度更快。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Assessing with design-era traffic underestimates accumulated damage, so fatigue cracks may start at rivet-hole edges and grow undetected; where corrosion and fatigue interact, cracks grow faster still. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b016-v13-s5","title":"耐久、維護與工程交接","titleEn":"Durability, maintenance and engineering handoff","description":"本階段聚焦「塗裝與腐蝕維護」與「工程遺產的修繕與交接」：先建立傳力機制與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Painting and corrosion maintenance\" and \"Repair and handover of engineering heritage\": build the load path and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b016-v13-33","title":"塗裝與腐蝕維護：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Painting and corrosion maintenance: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-32"],"objective":"說明「塗裝系統」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Paint system” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"雪梨港灣大橋處於海港環境，鹽霧與潮濕讓鋼材持續面臨腐蝕，而鉚接構造的板件搭接縫、鉚釘頭與角落正是積水與鹽分的位置。公開資料指出需要塗裝的鋼材面積約 485,000 平方公尺，每一道塗層約需 30,000 公升油漆，可見塗裝是持續性的大型工程，而不是偶爾的修補。塗裝系統的壽命取決於表面處理品質、膜厚與施工條件；舊漆層可能含鉛，噴砂與清除必須在封閉圍護與廢棄物管制下進行，以保護工人與港灣環境。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「塗裝系統」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"The bridge sits in a harbour environment where salt spray and humidity keep the steel under constant corrosion attack, and the lap seams, rivet heads and corners of riveted construction are exactly where water and salt collect. Public sources put the painted steel area at about 485,000 m², needing about 30,000 litres of paint per coat, showing that painting is a continuous major operation rather than occasional touch-up. Coating life depends on surface preparation, film thickness and application conditions; old layers may contain lead, so blasting and removal must happen inside containment with waste control to protect workers and the harbour. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Paint system” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：平均塗布率 = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Average spreading rate = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L.","failure":"常見誤解：「鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「塗裝系統」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Paint system”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-33-k1","title":"塗裝與腐蝕維護","titleEn":"Painting and corrosion maintenance","text":"雪梨港灣大橋處於海港環境，鹽霧與潮濕讓鋼材持續面臨腐蝕，而鉚接構造的板件搭接縫、鉚釘頭與角落正是積水與鹽分的位置。公開資料指出需要塗裝的鋼材面積約 485,000 平方公尺，每一道塗層約需 30,000 公升油漆，可見塗裝是持續性的大型工程，而不是偶爾的修補。","textEn":"The bridge sits in a harbour environment where salt spray and humidity keep the steel under constant corrosion attack, and the lap seams, rivet heads and corners of riveted construction are exactly where water and salt collect. Public sources put the painted steel area at about 485,000 m², needing about 30,000 litres of paint per coat, showing that painting is a continuous major operation rather than occasional touch-up.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「塗裝與腐蝕維護」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Painting and corrosion maintenance\" is correct?","options":["雪梨港灣大橋處於海港環境，鹽霧與潮濕讓鋼材持續面臨腐蝕，而鉚接構造的板件搭接縫、鉚釘頭與角落正是積水與鹽分的位置。","鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。","遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。"],"optionsEn":["The bridge sits in a harbour environment where salt spray and humidity keep the steel under constant corrosion attack, and the lap seams, rivet heads and corners of riveted construction are exactly where water and salt collect.","As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.","A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"雪梨港灣大橋處於海港環境，鹽霧與潮濕讓鋼材持續面臨腐蝕，而鉚接構造的板件搭接縫、鉚釘頭與角落正是積水與鹽分的位置。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"The bridge sits in a harbour environment where salt spray and humidity keep the steel under constant corrosion attack, and the lap seams, rivet heads and corners of riveted construction are exactly where water and salt collect. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b016-v13-34","title":"塗裝與腐蝕維護：定量估算","titleEn":"Painting and corrosion maintenance: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「塗裝系統」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Paint system” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：平均塗布率 = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L。若油漆體積固體分 50%，理論乾膜厚 DFT = 體積固體分×10/塗布率 = 50×10/16.2 ≈ 31 μm（未計損耗）；若目標系統總乾膜 250 μm，約需 8 道同等塗層的量。固體分與目標膜厚為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Average spreading rate = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L. With 50% volume solids, theoretical dry-film thickness DFT = volume solids×10/spreading rate = 50×10/16.2 ≈ 31 μm, ignoring losses; a 250 μm total system would need the equivalent of about 8 such coats. Solids content and target thickness are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：塗裝前檢查表面處理等級與鹽分殘留，施工時量測濕膜與乾膜厚度、環境溫濕度與露點；完成後抽測附著力，並建立分區塗裝紀錄，追蹤各區的劣化與重塗週期。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before painting check surface preparation grade and residual salts; during application measure wet and dry film thickness, ambient temperature, humidity and dew point; afterwards spot-test adhesion and keep zone-by-zone painting records to track deterioration and recoating cycles.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"平均塗布率 = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L。若油漆體積固體分 50%，理論乾膜厚 DFT = 體積固體分×10/塗布率 = 50×10/16.2 ≈ 31 μm（未計損耗）；若目標系統總乾膜 250 μm，約需 8 道同等塗層的量。固體分與目標膜厚為教學假設。","textEn":"Average spreading rate = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L. With 50% volume solids, theoretical dry-film thickness DFT = volume solids×10/spreading rate = 50×10/16.2 ≈ 31 μm, ignoring losses; a 250 μm total system would need the equivalent of about 8 such coats. Solids content and target thickness are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「塗裝與腐蝕維護」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Painting and corrosion maintenance\", which statement holds?","options":["拱只受壓，所以不需要考慮彎矩與受拉桿件。","平均塗布率 = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L。","鉸接支承一旦安裝完成，就會永遠自由轉動，不需要維護。"],"optionsEn":["An arch is only in compression, so bending and tension members need not be considered.","Average spreading rate = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L.","Once installed, a hinged bearing will always rotate freely without maintenance."],"answer":1,"explanation":"平均塗布率 = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Average spreading rate = 485,000 m² / 30,000 L ≈ 16.2 m²/L. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b016-v13-35","title":"塗裝與腐蝕維護：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Painting and corrosion maintenance: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「塗裝系統」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Paint system” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"塗裝前檢查表面處理等級與鹽分殘留，施工時量測濕膜與乾膜厚度、環境溫濕度與露點；完成後抽測附著力，並建立分區塗裝紀錄，追蹤各區的劣化與重塗週期。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before painting check surface preparation grade and residual salts; during application measure wet and dry film thickness, ambient temperature, humidity and dew point; afterwards spot-test adhesion and keep zone-by-zone painting records to track deterioration and recoating cycles. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：塗裝維護計畫應以分區劣化調查決定優先順序，規定表面處理、鹽分檢測與膜厚驗收標準，含鉛舊漆的移除須有圍護、監測與廢棄物管理方案；噴砂後先檢查鋼材損失與裂紋再塗裝。","observationEn":"Site practice: The painting programme should set priorities from zone-by-zone condition surveys, define surface preparation, salt testing and film-thickness acceptance, and require containment, monitoring and waste management for removing lead paint; after blasting, check section loss and cracks before recoating.","failure":"注意干擾：表面鹽分未清除就塗裝，塗膜下方很快起泡、剝落，腐蝕在漆膜下擴展；搭接縫的隙縫腐蝕產生膨脹力，可能把板件撐開、拉斷鉚釘頭，形成結構性損傷。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Painting over residual salt quickly blisters and lifts the film, spreading corrosion underneath; crevice corrosion in lap seams generates expansion forces that can pry plates apart and pop rivet heads, causing structural damage. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"塗裝前檢查表面處理等級與鹽分殘留，施工時量測濕膜與乾膜厚度、環境溫濕度與露點；完成後抽測附著力，並建立分區塗裝紀錄，追蹤各區的劣化與重塗週期。","textEn":"Before painting check surface preparation grade and residual salts; during application measure wet and dry film thickness, ambient temperature, humidity and dew point; afterwards spot-test adhesion and keep zone-by-zone painting records to track deterioration and recoating cycles.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"塗裝維護計畫應以分區劣化調查決定優先順序，規定表面處理、鹽分檢測與膜厚驗收標準，含鉛舊漆的移除須有圍護、監測與廢棄物管理方案；噴砂後先檢查鋼材損失與裂紋再塗裝。","textEn":"The painting programme should set priorities from zone-by-zone condition surveys, define surface preparation, salt testing and film-thickness acceptance, and require containment, monitoring and waste management for removing lead paint; after blasting, check section loss and cracks before recoating.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「塗裝與腐蝕維護」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Painting and corrosion maintenance\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","兩個半拱只要對準就能直接接上，溫度影響可以忽略。","塗裝前檢查表面處理等級與鹽分殘留，施工時量測濕膜與乾膜厚度、環境溫濕度與露點；完成後抽測附著力，並建立分區塗裝紀錄，追蹤各區的劣化與重塗週期。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","The two half-arches can simply be joined once aligned, and temperature can be ignored.","Before painting check surface preparation grade and residual salts."],"answer":2,"explanation":"塗裝前檢查表面處理等級與鹽分殘留，施工時量測濕膜與乾膜厚度、環境溫濕度與露點；完成後抽測附著力，並建立分區塗裝紀錄，追蹤各區的劣化與重塗週期。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before painting check surface preparation grade and residual salts; during application measure wet and dry film thickness, ambient temperature, humidity and dew point; afterwards spot-test adhesion and keep zone-by-zone painting records to track deterioration and recoating cycles. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b016-v13-36","title":"塗裝與腐蝕維護：失效診斷","titleEn":"Painting and corrosion maintenance: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「塗裝系統」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Paint system” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"表面鹽分未清除就塗裝，塗膜下方很快起泡、剝落，腐蝕在漆膜下擴展；搭接縫的隙縫腐蝕產生膨脹力，可能把板件撐開、拉斷鉚釘頭，形成結構性損傷。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Painting over residual salt quickly blisters and lifts the film, spreading corrosion underneath; crevice corrosion in lap seams generates expansion forces that can pry plates apart and pop rivet heads, causing structural damage. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：塗裝系統的壽命取決於表面處理品質、膜厚與施工條件；舊漆層可能含鉛，噴砂與清除必須在封閉圍護與廢棄物管制下進行，以保護工人與港灣環境。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Coating life depends on surface preparation, film thickness and application conditions; old layers may contain lead, so blasting and removal must happen inside containment with waste control to protect workers and the harbour.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「鋼橋只要定期刷一層新漆，就不會發生腐蝕損傷。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"As long as a steel bridge gets a fresh coat of paint regularly, corrosion damage cannot occur.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"表面鹽分未清除就塗裝，塗膜下方很快起泡、剝落，腐蝕在漆膜下擴展；搭接縫的隙縫腐蝕產生膨脹力，可能把板件撐開、拉斷鉚釘頭，形成結構性損傷。","textEn":"Painting over residual salt quickly blisters and lifts the film, spreading corrosion underneath; crevice corrosion in lap seams generates expansion forces that can pry plates apart and pop rivet heads, causing structural damage.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「塗裝與腐蝕維護」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Painting and corrosion maintenance\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["表面鹽分未清除就塗裝，塗膜下方很快起泡、剝落，腐蝕在漆膜下擴展；搭接縫的隙縫腐蝕產生膨脹力，可能把板件撐開、拉斷鉚釘頭，形成結構性損傷。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。"],"optionsEn":["Painting over residual salt quickly blisters and lifts the film, spreading corrosion underneath.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value."],"answer":0,"explanation":"表面鹽分未清除就塗裝，塗膜下方很快起泡、剝落，腐蝕在漆膜下擴展；搭接縫的隙縫腐蝕產生膨脹力，可能把板件撐開、拉斷鉚釘頭，形成結構性損傷。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Painting over residual salt quickly blisters and lifts the film, spreading corrosion underneath; crevice corrosion in lap seams generates expansion forces that can pry plates apart and pop rivet heads, causing structural damage. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b016-v13-37","title":"工程遺產的修繕與交接：機制與傳力路徑","titleEn":"Repair and handover of engineering heritage: mechanism and load path","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-36"],"objective":"說明「遺產保存與螺栓替換」如何影響雪梨港灣大橋的受力、變形或耐久表現，並畫出荷載的來源、傳遞路徑與支承邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement” governs force, deformation or durability in “Sydney Harbour Bridge”, and map where loads come from, how they travel and where they are supported.","instruction":"大橋在 1988 年被美國土木工程師學會列為國際歷史土木工程地標，並獲澳洲工程遺產的國家工程地標認定，2007 年建立保存管理計畫，現由新南威爾斯州交通部管理。遺產結構的修繕要在安全與真實性之間取得平衡：替換鉚釘時，現代高強度螺栓施工方便、預拉力可靠，但外觀與原有鉚接不同；以熱鉚復原則保存工藝，卻需要稀有技術。每一次修繕都會改變結構的組成，因此需要完整記錄替換了什麼、為什麼、用什麼材料，讓後來的工程師知道哪些部分已非原件。 師傅任務：以自由體圖或傳力路徑圖畫出荷載如何經過「遺產保存與螺栓替換」傳到支承或基礎，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"In 1988 the bridge was named an International Historic Civil Engineering Landmark by the American Society of Civil Engineers and a National Engineering Landmark by Engineering Heritage Australia; a conservation management plan was established in 2007, and the bridge is managed by Transport for NSW. Repairs to heritage structures balance safety with authenticity: modern high-strength bolts are easy to install with reliable preload but look different from rivets, while hot riveting preserves the craft yet needs rare skills. Each repair changes the fabric, so complete records of what was replaced, why and with what material are needed so later engineers know which parts are no longer original. Mentor task: draw a free-body or load-path diagram showing how loads pass through “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement” to the supports or foundation, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：以 M24、8.8 級高強度螺栓替換鉚釘時，預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN；摩擦係數 0.3、單一摩擦面時，每顆抗滑力約 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Replacing a rivet with an M24 grade 8.8 high-strength bolt gives a preload F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN; with a friction coefficient of 0.3 and one slip plane, each bolt resists about 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN of slip.","failure":"常見誤解：「遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在傳力圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your load-path diagram where it breaks down.","check":"傳力圖標明「遺產保存與螺栓替換」的荷載來源、傳遞路徑與支承；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The load-path diagram shows load sources, path and supports for “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-37-k1","title":"工程遺產的修繕與交接","titleEn":"Repair and handover of engineering heritage","text":"大橋在 1988 年被美國土木工程師學會列為國際歷史土木工程地標，並獲澳洲工程遺產的國家工程地標認定，2007 年建立保存管理計畫，現由新南威爾斯州交通部管理。遺產結構的修繕要在安全與真實性之間取得平衡：替換鉚釘時，現代高強度螺栓施工方便、預拉力可靠，但外觀與原有鉚接不同；以熱鉚復原則保存工藝，卻需要稀有技術。","textEn":"In 1988 the bridge was named an International Historic Civil Engineering Landmark by the American Society of Civil Engineers and a National Engineering Landmark by Engineering Heritage Australia; a conservation management plan was established in 2007, and the bridge is managed by Transport for NSW. Repairs to heritage structures balance safety with authenticity: modern high-strength bolts are easy to install with reliable preload but look different from rivets, while hot riveting preserves the craft yet needs rare skills.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「工程遺產的修繕與交接」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Repair and handover of engineering heritage\" is correct?","options":["遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。","大橋在 1988 年被美國土木工程師學會列為國際歷史土木工程地標，並獲澳洲工程遺產的國家工程地標認定，2007 年建立保存管理計畫，現由新南威爾斯州交通部管理。","雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。"],"optionsEn":["A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value.","In 1988 the bridge was named an International Historic Civil Engineering Landmark by the American Society of Civil Engineers and a National Engineering Landmark by Engineering Heritage Australia.","The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust."],"answer":1,"explanation":"大橋在 1988 年被美國土木工程師學會列為國際歷史土木工程地標，並獲澳洲工程遺產的國家工程地標認定，2007 年建立保存管理計畫，現由新南威爾斯州交通部管理。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"In 1988 the bridge was named an International Historic Civil Engineering Landmark by the American Society of Civil Engineers and a National Engineering Landmark by Engineering Heritage Australia; a conservation management plan was established in 2007, and the bridge is managed by Transport for NSW. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b016-v13-38","title":"工程遺產的修繕與交接：定量估算","titleEn":"Repair and handover of engineering heritage: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「遺產保存與螺栓替換」的關鍵量，並判斷跨度、荷載、溫度或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when span, load, temperature or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：以 M24、8.8 級高強度螺栓替換鉚釘時，預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN；摩擦係數 0.3、單一摩擦面時，每顆抗滑力約 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN。螺栓等級與摩擦係數為教學假設。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（例如增加 10%），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Replacing a rivet with an M24 grade 8.8 high-strength bolt gives a preload F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN; with a friction coefficient of 0.3 and one slip plane, each bolt resists about 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN of slip. Bolt grade and friction coefficient are teaching assumptions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example by +10%), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：替換前確認接頭的設計力與替換後的剛度差異，避免改變力量分配；螺栓施工以扭矩或轉角法控制預拉力並抽驗；每次修繕更新構件履歷資料庫，標明位置、材料、方法與日期，並由遺產管理單位確認符合保存計畫。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Before replacement confirm the joint's design forces and any stiffness change so force sharing is not altered; control preload by torque or turn-of-nut and spot-check it; after each repair update the component-history database with location, material, method and date, confirmed by the heritage manager as consistent with the conservation plan.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"重現模型中的數值（取整誤差在 ±5% 內），並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values (within ±5% rounding) and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"以 M24、8.8 級高強度螺栓替換鉚釘時，預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN；摩擦係數 0.3、單一摩擦面時，每顆抗滑力約 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN。螺栓等級與摩擦係數為教學假設。","textEn":"Replacing a rivet with an M24 grade 8.8 high-strength bolt gives a preload F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN; with a friction coefficient of 0.3 and one slip plane, each bolt resists about 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN of slip. Bolt grade and friction coefficient are teaching assumptions.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real structure, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「工程遺產的修繕與交接」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Repair and handover of engineering heritage\", which statement holds?","options":["鉚接接頭就像高強度螺栓摩擦接頭一樣，靠板件之間的摩擦傳力。","鋼拱在架設時就已經是拱，自己會撐住，不需要任何臨時支撐。","以 M24、8.8 級高強度螺栓替換鉚釘時，預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN。"],"optionsEn":["Riveted joints work like high-strength bolted friction joints, carrying load by friction between plies.","A steel arch already acts as an arch during erection and supports itself without temporary support.","Replacing a rivet with an M24 grade 8.8 high-strength bolt gives a preload F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以 M24、8.8 級高強度螺栓替換鉚釘時，預拉力 F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN；摩擦係數 0.3、單一摩擦面時，每顆抗滑力約 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Replacing a rivet with an M24 grade 8.8 high-strength bolt gives a preload F_p = 0.7·f_u·A_s = 0.7×800×353 ≈ 197.7 kN; with a friction coefficient of 0.3 and one slip plane, each bolt resists about 0.3×197.7 ≈ 59 kN of slip. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b016-v13-39","title":"工程遺產的修繕與交接：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Repair and handover of engineering heritage: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「遺產保存與螺栓替換」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"替換前確認接頭的設計力與替換後的剛度差異，避免改變力量分配；螺栓施工以扭矩或轉角法控制預拉力並抽驗；每次修繕更新構件履歷資料庫，標明位置、材料、方法與日期，並由遺產管理單位確認符合保存計畫。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Before replacement confirm the joint's design forces and any stiffness change so force sharing is not altered; control preload by torque or turn-of-nut and spot-check it; after each repair update the component-history database with location, material, method and date, confirmed by the heritage manager as consistent with the conservation plan. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：修繕方案應依保存管理計畫由結構工程師與遺產專家共同核定，明訂可接受的替換材料與外觀要求；交接文件包含構件履歷、檢查紀錄、塗裝分區、量測基準與遺產登錄要求，供未來的管理者延續。","observationEn":"Site practice: Repair schemes should be approved jointly by structural engineers and heritage specialists under the conservation management plan, stating acceptable replacement materials and appearance; handover documents include component histories, inspection records, painting zones, measurement baselines and heritage-listing requirements for future managers.","failure":"注意干擾：若在同一接頭混用鉚釘與高強度螺栓而未考慮勁度差異，力量會集中在較剛的螺栓，造成局部超載；修繕紀錄缺失時，後人無法分辨原件與替換件，評估時可能錯用材料性質。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、日照與施工荷重，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Mixing rivets and high-strength bolts in one joint without considering their different stiffness concentrates load on the stiffer bolts and overloads them locally; missing repair records leave later engineers unable to tell original from replaced parts, risking wrong material properties in assessment. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, sunshine and construction loads make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"替換前確認接頭的設計力與替換後的剛度差異，避免改變力量分配；螺栓施工以扭矩或轉角法控制預拉力並抽驗；每次修繕更新構件履歷資料庫，標明位置、材料、方法與日期，並由遺產管理單位確認符合保存計畫。","textEn":"Before replacement confirm the joint's design forces and any stiffness change so force sharing is not altered; control preload by torque or turn-of-nut and spot-check it; after each repair update the component-history database with location, material, method and date, confirmed by the heritage manager as consistent with the conservation plan.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"修繕方案應依保存管理計畫由結構工程師與遺產專家共同核定，明訂可接受的替換材料與外觀要求；交接文件包含構件履歷、檢查紀錄、塗裝分區、量測基準與遺產登錄要求，供未來的管理者延續。","textEn":"Repair schemes should be approved jointly by structural engineers and heritage specialists under the conservation management plan, stating acceptable replacement materials and appearance; handover documents include component histories, inspection records, painting zones, measurement baselines and heritage-listing requirements for future managers.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「工程遺產的修繕與交接」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Repair and handover of engineering heritage\"?","options":["替換前確認接頭的設計力與替換後的剛度差異，避免改變力量分配。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","載重試驗的目的是把橋加載到接近破壞，以證明它夠強。"],"optionsEn":["Before replacement confirm the joint's design forces and any stiffness change so force sharing is not altered.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","A load test aims to load the bridge close to failure to prove it is strong enough."],"answer":0,"explanation":"替換前確認接頭的設計力與替換後的剛度差異，避免改變力量分配；螺栓施工以扭矩或轉角法控制預拉力並抽驗；每次修繕更新構件履歷資料庫，標明位置、材料、方法與日期，並由遺產管理單位確認符合保存計畫。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Before replacement confirm the joint's design forces and any stiffness change so force sharing is not altered; control preload by torque or turn-of-nut and spot-check it; after each repair update the component-history database with location, material, method and date, confirmed by the heritage manager as consistent with the conservation plan. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b016-v13-40","title":"工程遺產的修繕與交接：失效診斷","titleEn":"Repair and handover of engineering heritage: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"prerequisiteIds":["b016-v13-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「遺產保存與螺栓替換」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Heritage conservation and bolt replacement” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"若在同一接頭混用鉚釘與高強度螺栓而未考慮勁度差異，力量會集中在較剛的螺栓，造成局部超載；修繕紀錄缺失時，後人無法分辨原件與替換件，評估時可能錯用材料性質。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體結構的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Mixing rivets and high-strength bolts in one joint without considering their different stiffness concentrates load on the stiffer bolts and overloads them locally; missing repair records leave later engineers unable to tell original from replaced parts, risking wrong material properties in assessment. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-structure safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：每一次修繕都會改變結構的組成，因此需要完整記錄替換了什麼、為什麼、用什麼材料，讓後來的工程師知道哪些部分已非原件。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Each repair changes the fabric, so complete records of what was replaced, why and with what material are needed so later engineers know which parts are no longer original.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「遺產橋梁只能原樣保存，任何修繕都會破壞其價值。」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A heritage bridge must be kept exactly as built, and any repair destroys its value.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b016-v13-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"若在同一接頭混用鉚釘與高強度螺栓而未考慮勁度差異，力量會集中在較剛的螺栓，造成局部超載；修繕紀錄缺失時，後人無法分辨原件與替換件，評估時可能錯用材料性質。","textEn":"Mixing rivets and high-strength bolts in one joint without considering their different stiffness concentrates load on the stiffer bolts and overloads them locally; missing repair records leave later engineers unable to tell original from replaced parts, risking wrong material properties in assessment.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]},{"id":"b016-v13-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「工程遺產的修繕與交接」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Repair and handover of engineering heritage\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","若在同一接頭混用鉚釘與高強度螺栓而未考慮勁度差異，力量會集中在較剛的螺栓，造成局部超載；修繕紀錄缺失時，後人無法分辨原件與替換件，評估時可能錯用材料性質。","雪梨港灣大橋兩端的巨大石砌橋塔承擔了拱的推力。"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Mixing rivets and high-strength bolts in one joint without considering their different stiffness concentrates load on the stiffer bolts and overloads them locally.","The massive stone pylons at each end of the bridge carry the arch thrust."],"answer":1,"explanation":"若在同一接頭混用鉚釘與高強度螺栓而未考慮勁度差異，力量會集中在較剛的螺栓，造成局部超載；修繕紀錄缺失時，後人無法分辨原件與替換件，評估時可能錯用材料性質。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Mixing rivets and high-strength bolts in one joint without considering their different stiffness concentrates load on the stiffer bolts and overloads them locally; missing repair records leave later engineers unable to tell original from replaced parts, risking wrong material properties in assessment. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v13s-nma-harbour-bridge","v13s-asce-sydney-harbour-bridge","v13s-bridge-museum-history","v13s-wiki-sydney-harbour-bridge"],"curriculumVersion":13,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000}};
